avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T12:43:29-07:00","id":1087291,"title":"","content":"Another gripe I noticed about the Kingdom of Jutland description on page 79, is the name of the king. <br /> The name they gave him is Harald Knudson, the problem is that Danish patronyms use the ending -sen not -son, so if it was to be &quot;correct&quot; Danish his name should be Harald Knudsen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2792-drucchi","name":"Drucchi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T13:06:24-07:00","id":1087305,"title":"","content":"Pg.79 I really like Empire of the Firebird name for Russia and other slavic countries( but you missed to mention Poland!! ) and most of the kingdoms have very mythological references<br /> <br /> Pg. 79 For a fix on Empire of the Caucasus<br /> <br /> #Azerbeijan, Georgia and Armenia(which is not mentioned in book) are in Caucasus BUT Turkmenistan, Kazakhstan and Uzbekistan are NOT in &quot;Caucasus&quot;. On the otherhand major part of Iran and Turkey already not in Caucasus. Please choose a name them refers them all:<br /> <br /> 1-Concept around Ottoman and Seljuq dynasty which sounds amazing and their regional area is obvious so &quot;Empire of the Oksoko/Twin Eagles&quot; is pretty usable for region which includes asia minor and central asia all together<br /> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oksoko\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oksoko</a> (another mythological bird from whole region, double headed eagle, thunder god) one head looks to the West, other one to the East.<br /> <br /> 2-Padishah Fae part is very nice but name starts with arabic continues celtic? Isnt &quot;Karim ibn Hassan of Gwydion&quot; way general? (Well, in turkish &quot;Gwydion'dan Hasano\u011flu Kerim&quot;; if you prefer a turkish kith grammar instead of arabic grammar)<br /> <br /> 3- Arabian Nights might be popular name for stories but its original name is &quot;One Thousand and One Nights&quot; and those stories includes Persian and even Far Eastern stories. Also there is a book called Legends of Dede Korkut which is popular among Turkey, Azerbeijan, Turkmenistan and rest of the Central Asia.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Book_of_Dede_Korkut\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fb/Kitab-%C4%B1_Dede_Korkut_ala-lisan-i_Ta%27ife-i_O%C4%9Fuzhan%2C_Dresden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Book_of_Dede_Korkut\" target=\"_blank\"> Book of Dede Korkut - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Book_of_Dede_Korkut\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Book_of_Dede_Korkut </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;romantic trappings of the One Thousand and One Nights and/or Legends of Dede Korkut&quot; if you wanna use smth inclusive<br /> <br /> Pg.5-6 &quot;He said he saw my bio about faerie stuff and invited for his Changeling the Dreaming chronicle. It didn\u2019t take too long to realize he is my&quot; &gt; Changeling: The Dreaming (colon : missed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10894,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 05-12-2017, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T16:00:20-07:00","id":1087375,"title":"","content":"On p99, the pooka kith frailty reads &quot;If he wishes to answer truthfully the player must make a Willpower roll (difficulty 8) and spend a point of Willpower.&quot;<br /> <br /> To keep their frailty in line with the boggan and troll frailties (the only other ones requiring Willpower rolls, the pooka frailty should omit the &quot;and spend a point of Willpower&quot; clause. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T18:36:50-07:00","id":1087444,"title":"","content":"p 234, one of the examples of gallain targets for Fae 4 is listed as &quot;neraka&quot; instead of naraka.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T18:43:16-07:00","id":1087446,"title":"","content":"P. 214, for the Oneiromancy 3 cantrip Dream Portal, it's unclear if you pop out of the dream in the Near Dreaming of the dreamer, or right next to the dreamer in the autumn world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T19:01:35-07:00","id":1087454,"title":"","content":"P. 218, under Pyretics Bunks &quot;just as the runs rises.&quot; I believe this should be &quot;just as the sun rises.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T19:48:36-07:00","id":1087474,"title":"","content":"p.116: Under 'Story possibility', it refers to the pooka overcoming their Birthright by spending a point of Willpower. However, it's a Willpower roll AND a point of Willpower (although, as Rabbit Pooka points out, it should probably just be the former and not the latter). If you're dropping the WP point expenditure as suggested, though, it'll need removing from the top of p.117 as well, where it's mentioned again, as well as other places (probably).<br /> <br /> I'd probably make a blanket rule that every kith with an Acuity gets a type of roll it can't botch, too, rather than overcomplicating the Acuity Birthright section by saying, 'Sometimes you can give your character this, but sometimes you can give them this AND THIS!' (because who isn't going to bundle the two things together if they're making their own kith?). But that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-03-2017, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T20:16:38-07:00","id":1087484,"title":"","content":"p.118: 'The demovoi is then bound that family', should be 'The demovoi is then bound to that family'<br /> <br /> In general: sometimes you have 'Autumn world' (mostly) and sometimes 'Autumn World' (p.123)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T20:21:06-07:00","id":1087486,"title":"","content":"Under 'Notable Members' in the house write-ups, it would probably make more sense to separate individuals by semi-colon rather than by comma alone. Thus:<br /> <br /> 'High Lord Li-Tilli, raised among werewolves and a consummate strategist, though now whispered to be slipping into Bedlam; The Mercy of Balor, a scarred and fearsome troll...' <br /> <br /> Etc. Separating them by commas makes it more difficult to parse. Alternatively, you can separate them by periods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T20:29:42-07:00","id":1087491,"title":"","content":"When you say 'eshu keepers' in the kith write-up, I'm assuming you meant 'eshu grumps'? I couldn't find any other reference to keepers, except where you describe grumps, and the preview we saw before used the placeholder seeming names, which I think included keepers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T20:34:01-07:00","id":1087492,"title":"","content":"Can you put the seeming modifiers on p.144 with the Tempers? Otherwise you're skimming four more pages for that info. At the very least, give us a heads up that they appear on p.148.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T20:42:30-07:00","id":1087493,"title":"","content":"P337, the term is &quot;in medias res&quot;, not &quot;in media res&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T20:44:50-07:00","id":1087494,"title":"","content":"Under the write-up for Holdings (p.170), it's probably worth mentioning that the Glamour is gained per night? Otherwise it could be per week or month.<br /> <br /> Resources and Treasures use different punctuation styles for explaining their levels. Resources lists levels as 'Sufficient. You have...' Treasures uses the format 'Common, rank one...' Abilities use 'Word: description...' for their format, so maybe use that? Really anal of me, I know, but it's such a beautiful book it should retain its consistency with text too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-03-2017, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T21:23:26-07:00","id":1087505,"title":"","content":"On pages 263-264: The mechanics on rhapsody it fails to say how much glamour is gained. All the setup and mechanics are in place but there isn't any indicator on the &quot;rewards&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13368-panzu","name":"Panzu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T21:56:23-07:00","id":1087512,"title":"","content":"On page 269 for Banality triggers it says that Ravaging or Rhapsodizing is a banality trigger, while on those specific sections it says that you just gain the point(s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","user":"zenten","date":". 05-04-2017, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T21:58:56-07:00","id":1087513,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">p. 207, First paragraph of the description of Holly-Strike: &quot;The activation roll for this cantrip doubles an attack roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> Should be &quot;The activation roll for this cantrip doubles AS an attack roll.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T22:20:06-07:00","id":1087519,"title":"","content":"p 371: Following are 20 Thallain kiths,<br /> <br /> There are only 19 listed and 19 illustrated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T22:30:44-07:00","id":1087520,"title":"","content":"am i going crazy or is Italy not covered at all in the world section?<br /> <br /> Ignore this, i see it now. Sleep deprevation is real everyone! it is real","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T01:42:06-07:00","id":1087574,"title":"","content":"P76 (France)<br /> <br /> <i>Conte Hillaire du Lille</i> --- <u>Comte</u> Hillaire <u>de</u> Lille<br /> <br /> <i>Lord Guy de Cheval of House Gwydion</i> --- <u>Seigneur Guy du Cheval de la Maison</u> Gwydion -- are you sure ? Cheval = Horse. It's a bit ridiculous <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <i>Consisting of the provinces of Provence-Alpes-C\u00f4te d\u2019Azur and Languedoc-Roussillon, along the Mediterranean Coast, this duchy is ruled by Lady Gen\u00e8ve of House Fiona</i>. --- Languedoc-Roussillon is now &quot;<u>Occitanie</u>&quot; since 2016.<br /> Gen\u00e8ve is not a french name, it's a Swiss city... I suggest &quot;Dame <u>Gueni\u00e8vre</u>&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2809-batro","name":"batro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T02:17:04-07:00","id":1087581,"title":"","content":"P33/sidebar p43 Kithain History : there's nothing about the Dark Ages Fae setting (the &quot;real&quot; past). It's sad <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Can you add some little explanation about the True Fae and the Mists please ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2809-batro","name":"batro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T02:38:57-07:00","id":1087588,"title":"","content":"Under Veiled Eyes, it would be useful to have some clarity about whether this befuddles technology too. Can we see the troll using Veiled Eyes on CCTV or does it suddenly turn to static or skip? Ditto with Veiled Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T02:54:58-07:00","id":1087593,"title":"","content":"For Time Dilation, are the ageing effects permanent on mortal creatures? If so, shouldn't fae and prodigals get some way to resist? If they're not, how long does the ageing last? My gut feeling is that it's easy to permanently age inanimate objects, but that PCs/NPCs should be able to resist or reverse these effects.<br /> <br /> How does this cantrip affect immortals? Vampires and old-school mummies don't age (the ones who didn't take the revised Spell of Life, that is). Risen, likewise. Maybe it manifests as aggravated damage instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-04-2017, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T03:19:00-07:00","id":1087598,"title":"","content":"Realms. If this meshes well with your design philosophy, could you clarify, which Realm (probably, either Props and Nature) is applicable for targeting radio signals, sound, light, software, such as viruses and apps, etc. and list few examples under appropriate Realms. <br /> <br /> I would be most thankful. No doubts many innovative changelings asked themselves the same thing. We live in 21st century, where concepts and information often can be much more important, than objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-04-2017, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T03:34:11-07:00","id":1087603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CameraObscura83</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1087520#post1087520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">am i going crazy or is Italy not covered at all in the world section?<br /> <br /> Ignore this, i see it now. Sleep deprevation is real everyone! it is real</div> </div> </div> </div>Relating to this, but not being an errata, is curious how in Iberia, Galicia is ignored, while being soooo related with the Hibernia (Ireland) as it is. At least I have a huge campaign with the Spanish North Western provinces as setting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13370-urtoroth","name":"Urtoroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13370_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T05:11:24-07:00","id":1087630,"title":"","content":"Animalistic Favor (p.187) says &quot;your mien possesses a minor animalistic feature from the below table&quot;, but the table is actually on p. 185.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T05:29:41-07:00","id":1087635,"title":"","content":"This is a matter of semantics, but under Contracts, most of the powers seem like modifications to the base cantrip, but they're called cantrips themselves, which is unclear. It makes it seem like a new cantrip is needed for each modification, when it isn't. Are bunks needed? I'm guessing not. So I think another word would be clearer. Really, they're levels of mastery rather than individual cantrips.<br /> <br /> Onto Dragon's Ire/Holly Strike: 'doubles an attack roll' should be 'doubles as an attack roll'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T06:22:52-07:00","id":1087648,"title":"","content":"Effigy seems a bit confusing to me, but it could just be my brain fog. When you say that Legerdemain + Realm stands in for Strength/Dexterity, is there a roll to cast the effect first, or do you just automatically swap Strength for Legerdemain + Realm? Does the physical action itself count as both bunk and activation? If you don't make a separate activation roll, the cantrip basically means you spend a point of Glamour to swap your Strength (or Dexterity) for Legerdemain + Realm for any one dice pool. In which case, it's simpler just to say that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T06:24:45-07:00","id":1087650,"title":"","content":"P144, the freebie point cost chart lists willpower as costing 2 freebie points. To keep this in line with the willpower cost listed in the other X20 books, the cost should be 1 freebie per willpower. V20, W20, and M20 all list willpower as costing 1 freebie point per.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:17:37-07:00","id":1087663,"title":"","content":"P. 302 has &quot;Increase time-based effects by trebling the required amount.&quot; I believe it should be &quot;Increase time-based effects by tripling the required amount.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:20:34-07:00","id":1087665,"title":"","content":"Does Geas require a roll? If so, what effect do successes have? If not, does it still require a bunk?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:21:36-07:00","id":1087666,"title":"","content":"P. 302 has &quot;Increase time-based effects by trebling the required amount.&quot; This should be &quot;Increase time-based effects by tripling the required amount.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:26:00-07:00","id":1087668,"title":"","content":"89 - I think the boggan stereotypes for &quot;Arcadian Sidhe&quot; and &quot;Autumn Sidhe&quot; have been reversed. &quot;They, perhaps more than any other, appreciate our service, and they have been here throughout the Interregnum. I respect them for that&quot; should be under the Autumn Sidhe heading and &quot;They still understand the old ways but they do not always understand our ways. Things have changed and they are going to need to learn to adapt&quot; should be under the Arcadian Sidhe heading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:40:14-07:00","id":1087677,"title":"","content":"Errors are listed with page number. The incorrect phrase is listed first, followed by my suggestion for the correction or change, usually listed in caps &amp; surrounded by asterisks. <br /> <br /> Pg 3: \u201cbut the only thing I can think about when I remember those days is much I felt my childhood was stolen\u201d should read but the only thing I can think about when I remember those days is is *HOW* much I felt my childhood was stolen\u201d<br /> <br /> Pg 3: \u201ca silver way to the world of unspoken beauty and frightening horrors, realm of ivory towers and forgotten dreams\u201d should read \u201c silver way to the world of unspoken beauty and frightening horrors *A* realm of ivory towers and forgotten dreams\u201d<br /> <br /> Pg 3 \u201dBut also it demonstrates the pain of being misunderstanded by others\u201d - should read :But also it demonstrates the pain of being *MISUNDERSTOOD* by others\u201d<br /> <br /> Pg3: \u201cgrowing is just forfuits\u201d - need a space between \u201cfor\u201d &amp; \u201cfruits\u201d<br /> <br /> Pg 3: \u201cwithout stopping to be sensible grow ups\u201d should read \u201cwithout stopping to be sensible GROWN ups\u201d<br /> <br /> Pg 3: : \u201cletting that banality consume us depends entirely of that curiosity\u201d should read \u201cletting that banality consume us depends entirely *ON* that curiosity\u201d<br /> <br /> Pg 3: \u201cit was so simple to fall in love for it.\u201d should read \u201cit was so simple to fall in love *WITH* it.\u201d<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12375-wratticusq","name":"Wratticusq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:51:57-07:00","id":1087686,"title":"","content":"The Nature Realm still has the problem of 'inorganic' matter at the first level. Arguably, soil is organic but would be presumably be covered by Nature 1. Maybe clarify that Nature 1 would affect the unliving soil itself but not the living organisms inside it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:57:45-07:00","id":1087689,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:MedievalSharp\">Errors are listed with page number. The incorrect phrase is listed first, followed by my suggestion for the correction or change, usually listed in caps &amp; surrounded by asterisks.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MedievalSharp\">Pg 4: \u201cI picked at a random one book from all possible core rules\u201d - This is just confusing. Perhaps it should read \u201cpicked at a random book from the possible core rules,\u201d leaving out the word *ONE*? Or maybe it should read \u201c*ONE RANDOM BOOK* from all possible core rules.\u201d</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12375-wratticusq","name":"Wratticusq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:58:03-07:00","id":1087690,"title":"","content":"Also, what happens when Glamour and Willpower drop to zero? The trait descriptions on pp.258-9 don't seem to say. They just say you bay trade in a permanent dot for more temporary points. In previous editions, zero Glamour meant your fae mien faded and you forgot your fae nature, IIRC. This might be elsewhere in the book, but a page reference might be good if so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:15:56-07:00","id":1087703,"title":"","content":"The rules for Freehold creation (p. 314-15) imply at Step Four a certain amount of permanent Glamour needs to be sacrificed (from personal Glamour, Chimera, or Treasures) to stabilize a balefire, but they never actually state the required amount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:17:43-07:00","id":1087704,"title":"","content":"Examples for using Arts within a main body of the description seem a bit confusing. Please, consider making them in Italics, different Font or something else of that merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> P. 217 Primal Art.<br /> <br /> As I understand second and fifth dots of this Art are pretty similar, the only difference being, former is a summoning process, of which you have no control over, while latter - a continuous, controlled and precise effect (but it doesn't summon anything).<br /> But <b>Eldritch Prime</b> lacks any mechanical teeth to it (like how much damage elements can cause and so on) and <b>Dance of the five kings </b>has no mention on how long it lasts. Maybe you should expand <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>System</b></span> section of the <b>EP</b> and reference it in the description of the <b>DotfK</b>. And I'm really not sure, whether <b>DotfK </b>is immediate or continuous, but if former, that's a bit tame, compared to <b>EP</b>. A bit of clarification on its duration would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-04-2017, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:19:03-07:00","id":1087705,"title":"","content":"185- The &quot;On Probation&quot; heading is on a separate page from the text it heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:19:46-07:00","id":1087706,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MedievalSharp\">Errors are listed with page number. The incorrect phrase is listed first, followed by my suggestion for the correction or change, usually listed in caps &amp; surrounded by asterisks. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MedievalSharp\">Pg 5: \u201cAt worst, it\u2019s the sound of dreams drying in a hostile world.\u201d should read \u201cAt worst, it\u2019s the sound of dreams *DYING* in a hostile world.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MedievalSharp\">Pg 5: \u201cWe all most certainly have at least once in our lives tought that our lives already written.\u201d should read \u201cWe all most certainly have at least once in our lives *THOUGHT* that our lives *ARE* already written.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MedievalSharp\">Pg 5: \u201ci had no idea about who he is\u201d - The word *I* should be capitalized. It should read, \u201c*I* had no idea who he *WAS*\u201d</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12375-wratticusq","name":"Wratticusq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:47:09-07:00","id":1087723,"title":"","content":"In the section on soaking, it's worth pointing out the possibility of chimerical armour (which wouldn't soak real damage). The section refers to armour soaking non-chimerical damage, which would, I think, only apply to real armour. Changelings, however, are more than likely to wear regular clothes with chimerical armour rather than actual suits of chainmail or what have you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:49:53-07:00","id":1087725,"title":"","content":"p.287: 'Chimerical, this weapon is always chimerical' should be Chimerical: This weapon is always chimerical' to match the other descriptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:59:57-07:00","id":1087733,"title":"","content":"Why are there soak difficulties for fire when fire is aggravated and therefore unsoakable? This problem has cropped up in other WoD books and I've never understood it. A Stamina + Survival roll to deal with smoke inhalation might make sense, but not to soak unsoakable damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T09:04:27-07:00","id":1087737,"title":"","content":"P. 174<br /> <br /> <b>Triggers </b><br /> End of the text block (right before the list): <i>(discussed anon)</i> - What's that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T09:05:42-07:00","id":1087740,"title":"","content":"Sometimes kith is used in the book to refer to an individual changeling, whereas Kithain or just 'changeling' might be more accurate (a kith being a splat, not an individual).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T09:08:53-07:00","id":1087743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1087733#post1087733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are there soak difficulties for fire when fire is aggravated and therefore unsoakable? This problem has cropped up in other WoD books and I've never understood it. A Stamina + Survival roll to deal with smoke inhalation might make sense, but not to soak unsoakable damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wearing armor allows the wearer to also soak <b>aggravated</b> and non-chimerical <b>lethal</b> damage, using the armor\u2019s rating as her total soak pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T09:10:24-07:00","id":1087744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1087743#post1087743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wearing armor allows the wearer to also soak <b>aggravated</b> and non-chimerical <b>lethal</b> damage, using the armor\u2019s rating as her total soak pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>The section discusses soaking with Stamina, so that needs fixing. It should say soaking with armour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T09:12:18-07:00","id":1087745,"title":"","content":"Another small thing: while the text says to mark aggravated damage with an asterisk, it doesn't seem to indicate how to mark bashing and lethal (/ and X, respectively). Old-time players will know this, but newbies might not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T09:20:00-07:00","id":1087748,"title":"","content":"p.461: 'Able to learn two Art' should be 'Able to learn two Arts'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T10:13:09-07:00","id":1087776,"title":"","content":"236: &quot;oak tree oak tree&quot; should just be &quot;oak tree&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T10:45:13-07:00","id":1087790,"title":"","content":"&quot;Queen Marsalie&quot; on the third column on page # 476 should be &quot;Queen Marsalie ni Fiona&quot; - if possible. Thank you either way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T10:57:37-07:00","id":1087797,"title":"","content":"P. 315 says &quot;Though the fae and the enchanted can observe chimera with all five senses, chimera cannot affect the mundane world except under special circumstances.&quot; However, earlier in the book those &quot;special circumstances&quot; are described as being just that no unenchanted mortal is watching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T11:50:13-07:00","id":1087832,"title":"","content":"Here's what I've got so far. Sorry if there are repeats:<br /> <br /> p. 14 &quot;A few lesser lords and ladies came with paperwork, which the lord of the tower signed <b>*it*</b> in a neat hand&quot;<br /> p. 16 &quot;like longing <b>[f]or</b> the beginning of winter.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">p. 64 &quot;dreams forged during the long years between the Shattering and the <b>[Resurgence].&quot;</b></span></span><br /> p. 105 Stereotypes &quot;On Satyrs \u2014 For all their passion, they <b>[know]</b> nothing of true love or romance.&quot;<br /> p. 106- &quot;When the Evanescence brought a new wave of <b>A[r]cadian</b> sidhe&quot;<br /> p 106 &quot;Some of these houses adjusted quickly to their new lives, but others held more extreme views about their role in relation to commoners and humans, which <b>cause[d]</b> further divisiveness.&quot;<br /> p. 106- &quot;The houses <b>[that returned]</b> in the Resurgence have had almost half a century to reestablish dominance and adjust to the new technologies and politics of the mortal world,&quot;<br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">p. 126- &quot;</span></span>Her son, Conchobhair, because a mighty warrior of great renown and unimpeachable honor.&quot; <b>sentence fragment</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">p. 133- <b>Countess</b> Glynann Jones, music producer to the stars and leader of the Finders,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">p. 134- and making last-ing connections that provide a continuing source for <b>Reverie</b>. <b>(seems like there are a lot of places where &quot;reverie and revelry are incorrectly interchanged</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">p. 134- toys and art supplies while quietly cultivating them for <b>Reverie.<br /> <br /> Also note that some of the items listed in the &quot;Revelry&quot; sections for various Kith seem to have more to do with interacting with others than finding glamour in oneself. See </b></span></span><b>Autumn Sidhe (109) and Wolpertinger (452) for examples that might need clarification.<br /> <br /> LASTLY: </b>I upgraded my pledge amount at the last second because I wanted hard copy. This should move my name from the Fledge section to the Changeling section. It currently reads &quot;David Tyberg ap Fiona, Baron of Battleground, protector of East Atlanta, Duchy of Willows Heart&quot; and I would like it listed thus:<br /> <br /> <b>The Rt. Hon. Lord Dimitri ap Fiona, Baron of Battlefield, protector of East Atlanta</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13307-dfunkmale","user":"Dfunkmale","date":". 05-04-2017, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13307-dfunkmale","name":"Dfunkmale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T15:51:23-07:00","id":1087962,"title":"","content":"Wrath of Kali Ma (p. 391): &quot;naraka have a partial immunity to fire; this damage type is <b>never </b>reduced to bashing and is at -1 difficulty to soak&quot;. I suppose this rule actually meant to say the damage is <b>always </b>reduced to bashing, otherwise it makes no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T15:53:40-07:00","id":1087964,"title":"","content":"Under Boggans, Arcadian and Autumn are reversed: On Arcadian Sidhe \u2014 They, perhaps more than any other, appreciate our service, and they have been here throughout the Interregnum. I respect them for that. On Autumn Sidhe \u2014 They still understand the old ways but they do not always understand our ways. Things have changed and they are going to need to learn to adapt<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:10:13-07:00","id":1087969,"title":"","content":"The replacement Nocker Birthright feels more like a parlor trick than the realm of master crafters. Maybe it's not fleshed out enough, I don't know, but without Infusion at least, they feel like they've had their teeth pulled (though I think it was probably a good idea to make it so they weren't the one Kith who could work the Dreaming like clay). Is there more to this I am missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:27:53-07:00","id":1087980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1087703#post1087703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for Freehold creation (p. 314-15) imply at Step Four a certain amount of permanent Glamour needs to be sacrificed (from personal Glamour, Chimera, or Treasures) to stabilize a balefire, but they never actually state the required amount.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could definitely be more explicitly stated. It's implied in &quot;Oathcircles or motleys may share the burden, each contributing 1 or more dots of Glamour until the intended rank is achieved.&quot;, but should more clearly indicate that it's one dot of Glamour per dot of Holdings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:39:20-07:00","id":1087988,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 360, Cold Iron Infusion - &quot;</b>If an augmented Prop is chimerical, it is destroyed when the cantrip\u2019s effects end.&quot;<br /> <br /> This should read &quot;an augmented weapon is chimerical&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:39:36-07:00","id":1087989,"title":"","content":"P 391 says &quot;. Additionally, due to their genesis, naraka cannot begin a game with the Background: Remembrance.&quot; I think that was a holdover from Denizens, as now in C20 the Naraka are way older than the Week of Nightmares (since the Week of Nightmares has been retconned).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T17:07:26-07:00","id":1088005,"title":"","content":"P29, &quot;For games involving the Kinain, or that skew further into urban fantasy, the October Daye series by Seanan McGuire is indispensable.&quot;<br /> <br /> Likely should be &quot;books&quot; rather than &quot;games&quot; here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:07:11-07:00","id":1088046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1087704#post1087704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Examples for using Arts within a main body of the description seem a bit confusing. Please, consider making them in Italics, different Font or something else of that merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Continuing this line. <br /> <br /> Some Arts have tiny sort of &quot;in character&quot; examples below their descriptions. Some - right above. Some Cantrips has no examples whatsoever.<br /> <br /> I don't want how much of it it intended, but standardizing it to some <i>degree </i>would be nice:<br /> <br /> Autump Cantrip's examples are above description. Except for Creeping shadows examples, which are in the same paragraph as description.<br /> All Chicanery Cantrips have their examples hidden within a first paragraph. <br /> Chronos 3-5 dots - examples below description. Effect and Cause has no examples. Backward Glance's example is within a first paragraph.<br /> Contract's Sanctified Words has no examples. Otherwise - above description.<br /> Dragon's Ire - above description.<br /> Legerdemain Cantrips has no examples, except for Effigy, that stuck within a first paragraph.<br /> Metamorphosis Cantrip Worms and Giants has no exampes. Others - above description.<br /> Oneiromancy Cantrips - below description.<br /> Primal Cantrip Eldritch Prime has no exampoles. Others - above description.<br /> Pyretics Cantrip Phoenix Song has no examples. Others - below description.<br /> Soothsay's 3 and 4 dots have no examples. Others - below description.<br /> Sovereign Cantrips - below description.<br /> Spring Cantrips - below description.<br /> Summer's dots 3-5 have no examples. Others <br /> Wayfare 1. 3-4 dots - examples are above. Quicksilver examples are below and within a description paragraph. Flicker Flash examples are below.<br /> Winter Cantrips - below description.<br /> <br /> Uhm. I hope someone takes a notice of this one. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:53:27-07:00","id":1088068,"title":"","content":"It was brought up in another thread that it might be an error the Mannikin Frailty makes no sense with the fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T20:36:52-07:00","id":1088084,"title":"","content":"pg 352: inventory of Akashic master lists &quot;stave&quot; instead of staff. Preceding page also refers to them as &quot;Akashi&quot; as a plural form, which I'm not sure really works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T21:46:03-07:00","id":1088101,"title":"","content":"pg 462, Bestowments, it says the enchanted mortal gets them but it isnt clear how many they get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T01:21:56-07:00","id":1088145,"title":"","content":"How long does Make It Right (the Nocker Birthright) work? I thought an earlier draft put a time-limit on such creations. Now it just says 'temporary' and 'improvised'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T03:45:15-07:00","id":1088181,"title":"","content":"Page 211, the Naming Cantrip &quot;Between the Lines&quot;, this part looks a bit wrong: &quot;Until the changeling can understand the real message in anything said or written, she cannot understand seek the intimate knowledge hidden within True Names.&quot; specifically the &quot;cannot understand seek&quot; part","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1862-inemeq","name":"iNemeq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:50:42-07:00","id":1088206,"title":"","content":"On the revised character sheet, the Nightmare track has a typo (&quot;Nighgmare&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:08:56-07:00","id":1088211,"title":"","content":"Page 223, the Augury Cantrip, the last line under system reads: &quot;Only one attempt can be made to find a specific fortune or destiny with his cantrip per story.&quot; I believe it should be &quot;this cantrip&quot; instead of &quot;his cantrip&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1862-inemeq","name":"iNemeq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:25:31-07:00","id":1088242,"title":"","content":"The Unseelie House entries still have references to their being involved in the Shadow Court, like they were in the previous edition, even though the Shadow Court is now a popular uprising against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:27:25-07:00","id":1088247,"title":"","content":"Also, South Carolina is listed as being the &quot;Duchy of Palmetto.&quot; Speaking as a native of the state, using &quot;Palmetto&quot; as a singular like that sounds really odd. The name should be the &quot;Duchy of the Palmetto,&quot; which matches the name of the state's highest civilian honor, the Order of the Palmetto.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:56:05-07:00","id":1088260,"title":"","content":"Page 50 says, &quot;Though initially only eight noble houses arrived from Arcadia to join House Scathach in the mortal world. . . &quot; And page 51 lists Liam as a returning house which contradicts the rest of the text.<br /> <br /> Beyond that technical feedback the more I think about the very strict framing of the Autumn Sidhe as Only being Scatthach and Liam combined with the &quot;Who knows if Arcadian Sidhe reincarnate&quot; framing basically erases wide swaths of a few house histories. Dougal and Fiona had several Sidhe stay behind in the canon and that frames a lot of their relationship with commoners now. If they died then the we don't know what happens to Arcadian Sidhe doesn't make any sense, and if they are included in the Autumn Sidhe dynamic then 1 sentence in the Arcadian Sidhe two page spread acknowledging the very rare Autumn Sidhe from other houses would go a long way towards allowing players to use the houses they love in this new setting. I personally have no preference on which way these old stragglers go (Autumn, or Arcadian who died centuries ago), but erasing them entirely when the houses get so little word count in C20 to fill in that social context hole is really awkward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:34:17-07:00","id":1088278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vikinzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088260#post1088260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 50 says, &quot;Though initially only eight noble houses arrived from Arcadia to join House Scathach in the mortal world. . . &quot; And page 51 lists Liam as a returning house which contradicts the rest of the text.<br /> <br /> Beyond that technical feedback the more I think about the very strict framing of the Autumn Sidhe as Only being Scatthach and Liam combined with the &quot;Who knows if Arcadian Sidhe reincarnate&quot; framing basically erases wide swaths of a few house histories. Dougal and Fiona had several Sidhe stay behind in the canon and that frames a lot of their relationship with commoners now. If they died then the we don't know what happens to Arcadian Sidhe doesn't make any sense, and if they are included in the Autumn Sidhe dynamic then 1 sentence in the Arcadian Sidhe two page spread acknowledging the very rare Autumn Sidhe from other houses would go a long way towards allowing players to use the houses they love in this new setting. I personally have no preference on which way these old stragglers go (Autumn, or Arcadian who died centuries ago), but erasing them entirely when the houses get so little word count in C20 to fill in that social context hole is really awkward.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not write that section and do not speak for the line as a whole, but my interpretation is that the majority (by whatever margin) were from those Houses, not <i>all. </i> Autumn sidhe aren't necessarily limited to just those two. Nobles from any House might have chosen to remain behind with their subjects, their peers, their friends, when the trods started closing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:42:14-07:00","id":1088309,"title":"","content":"I saw several areas in the book that specifically state only Scatthach and Liam stayed behind. I did a word search for Autumn Sidhe to find any reference to the occasional Autumn Sidhe from other houses and couldn't find any. I am glad they're omission wasn't on purpose, but given that in previous books the sidhe who stayed behind from houses other than Scatthach did not reincarnate I really feel like the current text needs a couple words of framing especially given the no one knows what happens to Arcadian Sidhe plot hook. I like that hook but it makes things like the slow death of the Dougal Sidhe who stayed behind and the gradual inheritance of the house by commoners confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:42:53-07:00","id":1088310,"title":"","content":"On Page 91 for the Clurichaun frailty it says banality is triggered after a week away from their hordes, but doesn't indicate how rapidly it acrues. Since it's a prolonged separation I think most people will want to know how rapidly the banality collects after that first week. I would assume 1 a week, but confirmation would be really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:10:49-07:00","id":1088321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vikinzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088309#post1088309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw several areas in the book that specifically state only Scatthach and Liam stayed behind. I did a word search for Autumn Sidhe to find any reference to the occasional Autumn Sidhe from other houses and couldn't find any. I am glad they're omission wasn't on purpose, but given that in previous books the sidhe who stayed behind from houses other than Scatthach did not reincarnate I really feel like the current text needs a couple words of framing especially given the no one knows what happens to Arcadian Sidhe plot hook. I like that hook but it makes things like the slow death of the Dougal Sidhe who stayed behind and the gradual inheritance of the house by commoners confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the impression that it was an ST call, but now that you put it like this im not surehow i got that impression....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:24:23-07:00","id":1088327,"title":"","content":"Don't know if it's been already adressed but the River Hags template miss the Unleashing section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:31:58-07:00","id":1088331,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:verdana\">P236, &quot;<span style=\"font-size:10px\">The base difficulty of the cantrip is 8, raised to 9 by the inclusion of the Time Realm, but then reduced <i><u><b>by the by</b></u></i> \u20132 for the bunk, giving the cantrip a final difficulty of 7.&quot;<br /> <br /> The second by should be removed.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T09:33:33-07:00","id":1088333,"title":"","content":"Page 87 says a Fae reduces the difficulty of all cantrips involving their affinity realm by 1. Page 117 says it's only when the realm is primary, but then immediately gives examples of realms that are always secondary (scene, time). I suspect 117 should be changed to any time the affinity realm is included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:01:25-07:00","id":1088350,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I just found a little bit of text in the Fionna write-up that acknowledges that some of their house stayed behind. It's in their exile write-up. I still think one or two sentences of more generic invocation would help avoid confusion, but I do appreciate that there is some text holding that space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:16:58-07:00","id":1088356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vikinzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088333#post1088333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 87 says a Fae reduces the difficulty of all cantrips involving their affinity realm by 1. Page 117 says it's only when the realm is primary, but then immediately gives examples of realms that are always secondary (scene, time). I suspect 117 should be changed to any time the affinity realm is included.</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly since Arcadian Sidhe have Time as their Affinity realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:21:13-07:00","id":1088359,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this is a repeat:<br /> <br /> on Page 212 it notes that reweaving can't change the physical form of a living creature, but then goes on to give examples of doing just that with it (turning a cat into a gun, or a werewolf into a puppy)<br /> <br /> Otherwise, so, on page 103, it felt like the book was about to finally fix what I've always found to be the creepy, roofieish quality of Gift of Pan, saying this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">The Gift of Pan doesn\u2019t force anyone to partake in sex or any other activity, but removes inhibitions that might normally keep someone from indulging. Rather than creating a new passion, the Gift of Pan removes the barriers of social convention that might otherwise prevent someone from being able to completely surrender to an action of passion or revelry. </span> </div> </div> </div>But the entry then closes with this, which seems to entirely contradict it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Those failing a Banality or Willpower roll (difficulty 8) find themselves helpless to resist indulging their secret desires. </span> </div> </div> </div>It could use clearer wording maybe? Because it seems to contradict what comes before it pretty hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:29:46-07:00","id":1088369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vikinzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088309#post1088309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw several areas in the book that specifically state only Scatthach and Liam stayed behind. I did a word search for Autumn Sidhe to find any reference to the occasional Autumn Sidhe from other houses and couldn't find any. I am glad they're omission wasn't on purpose, but given that in previous books the sidhe who stayed behind from houses other than Scatthach did not reincarnate I really feel like the current text needs a couple words of framing especially given the no one knows what happens to Arcadian Sidhe plot hook. I like that hook but it makes things like the slow death of the Dougal Sidhe who stayed behind and the gradual inheritance of the house by commoners confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any sidhe who stayed behind underwent the Changeling Way and are now Autumn sidhe who reincarnate as the other kiths do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:34:47-07:00","id":1088373,"title":"","content":"If it helps, it says this under House Gwydion on 131, when talking about the whole &quot;they left because they were commanded by the High King&quot; bit (which I'm pleased to see got carried over from Shining Host, unrelated note)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">House Gwydion first came into power shortly after the Sundering, claiming lands and titles abandoned by the sidhe returning to Arcadia. In this period of chaos and fear, the strong guiding hand of Gwydion reassured its subjects, who looked to the honesty and dignity of their new lieges for guidance. House Gwydion ruled wisely and fairly until the Shattering, when they heeded the High King\u2019s orders to retreat from the rising sea of Banality. <b>While many noble houses remained behind in part or in full</b>, House Gwydion returned to Arcadia in near totality, forced to abandon the lands they once protected. </span> </div> </div> </div>Bolded part relevant. Maybe put that note somewhere more prominently? Under the Autumn Sidhe kith section itself maybe. Easier not to miss that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T11:36:30-07:00","id":1088398,"title":"","content":"Faerie Eternity, p. 186: &quot;As long as your fae seeming is active, you will age at one-tenth that of a normal human or changeling <b>and remain a childling</b>&quot;. Since in C20 Seemings are supposed to be a reversible/switchable preferred mental/spiritual condition for changelings rather than a strict reflection of their physical age, for all characters with this Merit to be forced in the same Seeming just seems wrong. After all, in this edition you may easily have 50-year-old Childlings and 12-year-old Grumps. On the other hand, the price tag for the Merit feels just right.<br /> <br /> Preventing Aging, p. 47. The paragraph would be much better if rewritten to explictly state the only tried-and-true method for changelings to extend their lifespan is spend time in a freehold <b>or the Dreaming</b>. After all, freeholds do work because they are close to the Dreaming and provide abundant, steady sources of Glamour, and the Dreaming itself works much better at both of these things than any balefire. So the Dreaming should be explictly mentioned to be just as effective as freeholds to extend the lifespan of changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-05-2017, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:04:57-07:00","id":1088506,"title":"","content":"Page 42: &quot;...and many fae are picked off before they can ever fully realize themselves fully.&quot;<br /> Should be: &quot;...and many fae are picked off before they can ever fully realize themselves.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T18:13:29-07:00","id":1088576,"title":"","content":"Uhm, not sure about using this thread correctly, but...<br /> <br /> Would you consider leaving a couple of blank pages near the end of the physical book for House Rules purposes? I solemnly promise to be respectful!<br /> <br /> It's just, that Changeling was always a multifaceted game, due to its presentation, multiple writers or flaws, that it was fine-tuned for each individual Storyteller and gaming group, one way or another.<br /> <br /> Just consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-06-2017, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T19:01:25-07:00","id":1088589,"title":"","content":"P. 367 says &quot; In addition, the Undone gains a Derangement of the Storyteller\u2019s choice.&quot;, but Derangements have been (thankfully) removed as a system concept in Changeling 20th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T02:27:50-07:00","id":1088668,"title":"","content":"Page 50 - The Houses - contains a brief write-up of all houses but not House Danaan, even though it is included as a playable House later in the book.<br /> <br /> Page 107 - Stereotypes for Arcadian Sidhe are given by Regan ferth Cwentryth. This should be Regan fer<b>ch</b> Cwentryth. (&quot;Ferch&quot; not &quot;ferth&quot; is the female version of &quot;ap&quot; in Welsh, means &quot;daughter of&quot;).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-06-2017, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T02:53:03-07:00","id":1088671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088359#post1088359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this is a repeat:<br /> <br /> on Page 212 it notes that reweaving can't change the physical form of a living creature, but then goes on to give examples of doing just that with it (turning a cat into a gun, or a werewolf into a puppy)<br /> <br /> Otherwise, so, on page 103, it felt like the book was about to finally fix what I've always found to be the creepy, roofieish quality of Gift of Pan, saying this:<br /> <br /> <br /> But the entry then closes with this, which seems to entirely contradict it:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It could use clearer wording maybe? Because it seems to contradict what comes before it pretty hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>My feeling is that the Birthright should reduce inhibitions, in the same way alcohol might, but that trying to make someone do anything that goes against their core nature or desires (e.g., date rape) automatically fails. If a person doesn't want to do something, they won't. If they want to, but feel too self-conscious normally, this Birthright is the social lubricant they need to loosen up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:13:26-07:00","id":1088674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088369#post1088369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any sidhe who stayed behind underwent the Changeling Way and are now Autumn sidhe who reincarnate as the other kiths do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly glad to hear that. I just really hope there are future books that cover the houses so the sections that center on Sidhe staying behind and slowly dying out like Dougal can get a new pass that fits with this setup. I honestly prefer this setup, it just leaves some holes in existing canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12419,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","user":"vikinzer","date":". 05-06-2017, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:23:19-07:00","id":1088677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088671#post1088671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My feeling is that the Birthright should reduce inhibitions, in the same way alcohol might, but that trying to make someone do anything that goes against their core nature or desires (e.g., date rape) automatically fails. If a person doesn't want to do something, they won't. If they want to, but feel too self-conscious normally, this Birthright is the social lubricant they need to loosen up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the problem with this is that it assumes that lowered inhibitions can make people make decisions that are risky or that their sober selves would not be comfortable with. Drunken consent may not be genuine consent - someone may still rightly feel violated if they slept with someone only because that person got them drunk (even if they secretly wanted to).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, honestly, that's just what the birthright <i>is</i>. Fae <i>are</i> creepy sometimes. Cantrips can also be used in really violating, gross ways too. Since the birthright has applications that <i>aren't </i>gross, I don't have a problem with the fact it <i>can</i> be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-06-2017, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:23:28-07:00","id":1088678,"title":"","content":"On page 146 there is a gender pronoun change in a single sentence. &quot;Did he ever enchant anyone he knew, or otherwise try to let them in on her secret?&quot;. I like the pronoun variety but changing in a single sentence doesn't seem intentional.<br /> <br /> Page 176 The rules for gaining banality say &quot;When a character is triggered, the player rolls her Glamour at a difficulty of 8. If the roll fails, the character gains a Banality point. If the roll is a botch, the character gains a point of Banality for every one rolled&quot;. I just wanted to be sure the intent was for a failure and a single botch to have the same impact. Given that botches require no successes and 1s to be present this seems unusually forgiving. I figured botches would be 1 banality plus the number of 1s rolled.<br /> <br /> Page 185 On Probation has an animal trait advantage chart instead of text for that flaw.<br /> <br /> Page 194 The text, &quot;Voluntarily replace at least 3 dice with Night-mare Dice&quot; implies there is an ability to a gain from replacing more than 3 dice. I didn't see anything that detailed a benefit for replacing more than 3 dice. If you can only do this once the words 'at least' should be removed. If you can do this multiple times a few words indicating so on 274 would provide clarity.<br /> <br /> Page 207 The rules for Holly Strike say it doubles an attack roll, but it seems like it means doubles as an attack role.<br /> <br /> Page 263. I can't find a system for how much glamour Rhapsody actually creates per success on the artist role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T05:11:01-07:00","id":1088708,"title":"","content":"I re-read this and realized I misunderstood things. The one small question I have wasn't appropriate for the errata thread, but I didn't see a delete option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12419,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","user":"vikinzer","date":". 05-06-2017, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T05:47:43-07:00","id":1088714,"title":"","content":"Page 67 - The Duchy of Blue Grasses - this is described as being ruled by a Kinain Duke. The next line talks about his fae mien. I haven't read the appendix on the Enchanted yet, so this could be a C20 change, but I don't think Kinain have a fae mien? Even if I'm wrong, there's nothing in the write up about the social implications of having a Kinain Duke or how that could come about. It's a fascinating idea, but with no textual acknowledgement of how extraordinarily unusual it is, it feels confusing and like a possible typo?<br /> <br /> Page 68 - West Virginia is listed as part of both the Duchy of Winterhold and the Duchy of Dogwood with no clarification as to how it's carved up.<br /> <br /> Also, under the Duchy of Dogwood write up, it refers to David Ardry as a &quot;young king&quot;, which seems inaccurate given the advancements of the metaplot. It then describes a secret Shadow Court freehold, but given the changes to the nature of the Shadow Court in C20, should this be the Black Court instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T11:50:58-07:00","id":1088809,"title":"","content":"pgs 277-279, there appears to be no entry for a standard punch among the combat maneuvers.<br /> pg 286: While possibly more of a word choice than an error, the entry for broadsword is typically what's known as a bastard sword in popular culture. Less subjectively, the header for improvised and unusual weapons is not bolded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-06-2017, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T17:21:04-07:00","id":1088913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088677#post1088677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think the problem with this is that it assumes that lowered inhibitions can make people make decisions that are risky or that their sober selves would not be comfortable with. Drunken consent may not be genuine consent - someone may still rightly feel violated if they slept with someone only because that person got them drunk (even if they secretly wanted to).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, honestly, that's just what the birthright <i>is</i>. Fae <i>are</i> creepy sometimes. Cantrips can also be used in really violating, gross ways too. Since the birthright has applications that <i>aren't </i>gross, I don't have a problem with the fact it <i>can</i> be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem people may have with this birthright is they mistakenly equate it with being roofied or made drunk against their will, which IMO goes against the intent of the authors. I prefer to equate it with being presented with the opportunity to indulge in an incredibly appealing sensual stimulus. Think of an incredibly sexy and charming person of the gender you find attractive walking up to you, with the food you most fancy in the world, and the music you prefer playing. In normal conditions, the temptation to indulge would be overwhelming, yet if the person truly wants to, they can resist and turn down the offer.<br /> <br /> On your second point, yes, the Dreaming absolutely does not play favorites for humans or their ethical expectations, nor it can reasonably expected to. It does not have a problem with the Fomorian Dream getting dominant again, and it is so vast and ancient it spans the whole psychic imprint of history and the world, so it would be silly to expect it would pay special regard to 21st century ideas about consent. Given how many of its features reflect the archetypes of power, violence, domination, and seduction, and how much these archetypes are fundamental to human/cosmic collective consciousness, It is only to be expected that several of the manifestations it spawns may have creepy and violating implications. We may choose not to give explicit representation to these aspects at our tables, but it is unreasonable to expect they wouldn't exist somewhere in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-06-2017, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:20:44-07:00","id":1088977,"title":"","content":"P.368 on - None of the Thallain, Dark-kin, Nunnehi, Menehune, or Inanimae have Revelry conditions. Is there some reasoning behind this, or was it a mistake?<br /> <br /> P.385 - Denizens and the Autumn World: Methods of Dark-kin entering the Autumn World are referenced, but no real rules for it are given.<br /> <br /> P.394 - In the Nunnehi Tribes section, it seems that the Midwest has been omitted from the list of regions.<br /> <br /> P.418 - Gathering Medicine: It's mentioned that Winter/War Legacies regain Mana/Medicine by hunting and killing animals and fish, but it's never explained how this functions. Also, the tribal kiths cannot obtain Mana/Medicine from <i>any</i> form of artistic endeavor, not even those of First Peoples' origins; was this intentional?<br /> <br /> P.421 - Hsien: While it is repeatedly mentioned, nowhere in this section is it explained how Hsien assume their Wani form.<br /> <br /> P.423 - In 'Advantages: Luck, Curse, &amp; Backgrounds', it says Hsien use a modified form of the Retinue Background, but it isn't explained with the Backgrounds on P.425.<br /> <br /> P.425 - Kwannon-jin: The list naming the types of Hirayanu leaves out the Hanumen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 05-06-2017, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T23:01:46-07:00","id":1089012,"title":"","content":"on page 89... the boggans opinions on Arcadian and autumn Sidhe seem to be Switched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T00:55:54-07:00","id":1089037,"title":"","content":"Are there additional character sheets for the Inanimae, Dark-Kin, Nunnehi, and Hsien? Seems like the basic sheet doesn't cover these quite well enough...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12635-tomofviledarkness","name":"TomOfVileDarkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T02:16:00-07:00","id":1089046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088913#post1088913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the problem people may have with this birthright is they mistakenly equate it with being roofied or made drunk against their will, which IMO goes against the intent of the authors. I prefer to equate it with being presented with the opportunity to indulge in an incredibly appealing sensual stimulus. Think of an incredibly sexy and charming person of the gender you find attractive walking up to you, with the food you most fancy in the world, and the music you prefer playing. In normal conditions, the temptation to indulge would be overwhelming, yet if the person truly wants to, they can resist and turn down the offer.<br /> <br /> On your second point, yes, the Dreaming absolutely does not play favorites for humans or their ethical expectations, nor it can reasonably expected to. It does not have a problem with the Fomorian Dream getting dominant again, and it is so vast and ancient it spans the whole psychic imprint of history and the world, so it would be silly to expect it would pay special regard to 21st century ideas about consent. Given how many of its features reflect the archetypes of power, violence, domination, and seduction, and how much these archetypes are fundamental to human/cosmic collective consciousness, It is only to be expected that several of the manifestations it spawns may have creepy and violating implications. We may choose not to give explicit representation to these aspects at our tables, but it is unreasonable to expect they wouldn't exist somewhere in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to derail the thread too much, so I'll make this my final response, but basically, I don't think authorial intent matters much if it's easy to read it in another way. Your examples might still be cruel in various contexts. Tempting an alcoholic to drink, for instance. The Satyr might not be aware, but it could still be damaging. Or perhaps someone consents to sex they would not have otherwise consented to - perhaps a libidinous desire exists but sleeping with your spouse's boss is still a terrible idea. There really is no getting around the fact that the birthright can cause you to do things you may very much WANT to do but will still have dire and dramatic consequences after the fact. <br /> <br /> However, as I've said, I don't mind because it's not inherently exploitative. If the ONLY way for Satyr players to use the Gift of Pan was creepy then there would be a problem. But I don't believe that's the case.<br /> <br /> With regards to 21st century ideas about consent, well, it's a 21st century game, played by 21st century humans. I think the actual problem is that what constitutes consent in the 21st century is still disputed, particularly by certain less savoury &quot;alt-right&quot; aligned parts of gamer subculture.<br /> <br /> My position is that the Gift of Pan has the inherent <i>capacity </i>to be gross, but that this isn't a problem as long as everyone is on the approximately the same page about where the line of &quot;gross&quot; lies and what topics they're comfortable exploring in the game.<br /> <br /> Others - as I understand it - feel that they are already at times besieged by an unsafe environment and find the Gift of Pan's potential grossness a red flag that will make awkward situations more likely in a game environment.<br /> <br /> Then we get into the matter of gaming in spaces that feel safe to us, and it's easier for me to say that I wouldn't game with jerks like that because I have a realworld gaming group. Others have to play with strangers online and so are more leery of ethical grey areas like this. I understand that, and I also understand that the whole &quot;but it's just what you secretly wanted!&quot; aspect of the birthright could make it more difficult to call out as creepy (whereas using dictum to demand someone do something is inarguably a violation of free will so one could assume the game would treat it as such). But ultimately I still feel like there are many, many other cantrips and abilities in this game (indeed in most games) that can be used in gross ways, that the debate over the Gift of Pan is in part a flashpoint for wider concerns about gaming culture and how to negotiate what's off limits and how to handle uncomfortable material.<br /> <br /> I still mostly come down on the side of C20 not being responsible for that, and the answer not being to make the orgy fae less good at orgies, but instead just realistically dealing with when it's okay to start an orgy and/or dealing with the fallout when it wasn't if a gaming group is comfortable exploring that.<br /> <br /> I'm not unsympathetic to the alternate opinion, though. As I said, I'm conscious that I am speaking from the perspective of someone who has a gaming group she feels fairly comfortable with.<br /> <br /> Anyway - sorry for the derail. It's an interesting question and I didn't want to let it lie. Maybe we should start another thread if we want to continue the discussion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-07-2017, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T05:48:53-07:00","id":1089087,"title":"","content":"I just realized there Selkie shape changing isn't actually listed in their birthrights. They have two birthrights, but neither one is shape changing. Given that we see a Selkie allow someone else to use their skin in the anthology this really needs systems. Can you do this with a just enchanted, do they need to have a Fae soul, what does it cost especially if done for someone else? The shape changing is obviously described in the flavor, but not as an actual listed power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12419,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","user":"vikinzer","date":". 05-07-2017, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T05:54:05-07:00","id":1089090,"title":"","content":"There's a slight inconsistency here. Unless it doesn't worry you.<br /> <br /> P79:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i><b>The Kingdom of Dalarna (Norway and Sweden) </b></i><br /> ...<br /> Here, as well as in The Isle of Snow\ufb02akes and the Kingdom of Jutland, Seelie fae refer to themselves </span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">as </span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><b>lios </b><b>alfar</b></b> (faeries of light), while Unseelie fae call themselves <b>svart </b><b>alfar</b> (faeries of darkness)</span> </div> </div> </div>P381:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i><b>Sevartal</b></i></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Svart%C3%A1lfar\" target=\"_blank\">Svart\u00e1lfar</a> </span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> = S<span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\">e</span>vart</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">\u00e1</span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">l<span style=\"color:#808080\">far</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">And from how you're framing it, </span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Thallain</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> has nothing to do with Unseelie. Unseelie is just darker and edgier version of Seelie to </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Thallain's</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> sadistic murderous psychopaths.</span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-07-2017, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T06:32:13-07:00","id":1089100,"title":"","content":"All the Thallains entries seem to lack a realm affinity. Is it normal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:26:50-07:00","id":1089130,"title":"","content":"About Neustria (p. 76).<br /> <br /> I always figured that the Duchy of '&quot;Bayeaux&quot; was named after the medieval town in Normandy which proper spelling is &quot;Bayeux&quot; (without the second &quot;a&quot;).<br /> <br /> Also, the name of the duke is Conte Hillaire du Lille.<br /> <br /> First, it should be spelled &quot;Comte&quot; (Count) and not &quot;Conte&quot; (which means a &quot;tale&quot;, like a fairy tale).<br /> <br /> And more important: Bayeux is in western France and this area has a very different history and dream I would say than northern France where Lille is located.<br /> <br /> About Burgundy: I concur with the forum member who said that Lord Guy de Cheval sounds a little bit ridiculous, which is not a good idea a for sidhe.<br /> <br /> Lady Gen\u00e8ve is not French. I also concur with the forum member who proposed instead Gueni\u00e8vre.<br /> <br /> Aquitaine: since it is an independent desmene, then it should not be a duchy, because a duke is a war lord in the service of a king. Rather, Aquitaine should be a principality, and Rathesmere the Prince of Aquitaine (which would have a nice ring to it, as it recalls the Hundred Years War and would explain why Aquitaine is independent from Neustria).<br /> <br /> Finally, a last question: you seem to have had the rights to use the kiths from the Monde des T\u00e9n\u00e8bres: France book, so why not use the duchies and counties and kingdoms from it too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","user":"mattboggan","date":". 05-07-2017, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:34:25-07:00","id":1089138,"title":"","content":"About Greece (p. 79): There is a reference of the &quot;ancient Greek Empire&quot;. This puzzles me. What empire? Is this Alexander's Empire (the name &quot;Hellenic Empire in the header led me to believe this, since the &quot;Hellenic&quot; period began after the death of Alexander)? If so, it should be clearly stated, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:37:09-07:00","id":1089140,"title":"","content":"About Africa (p. 80): no reference is made of the Blue Sands eshu (Egypt) even if there were mentioned in KB: Nockers (character template for the AEthernaute) and in a character template released on the Internet for the keremet (Denizens of the Dreaming).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T08:26:40-07:00","id":1089167,"title":"","content":"This is a lot more in the systems weeds than I am totally comfortable getting in this thread, so if this is really not appropriate for this stage please feel free to ignore. That said here goes.<br /> <br /> The fact that Inanimae can only unleash makes them dramatically more susceptible to Bedlam than normal Changelings. That seems like a huge intrinsic flaw. Was this intentional? I've always seen Bedlam described as glamour's toxicity on a Changelings human soul, which the Inanimae don't have. While I'm definitely not for wiping bedlam out for the Inanimae because that's huge and structural, making them more susceptible to it than meat Changelings seems like it would make long term play difficult difficult for Inanimae and strange thematically. It's easy enough at my table to say &quot;You are better at unleashing since it's all you do, you only get nightmare on a failure or botch&quot;, but I did want to see if this dynamic was intended or if I'm missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T09:24:57-07:00","id":1089205,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this one has already been mentioned:<br /> <br /> p. 26a:<br /> <br /> &quot;it\u2019s best for each player to have a set of 10 or so, but you can [<b>go</b>?] by with fewer&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:43:38-07:00","id":1089283,"title":"","content":"Page 72 - Duchy of White Trillium write up - &quot;Lady Serena of House Dareann&quot; - Daireann is misspelled.<br /> <br /> Also the Nunavut entry starts with &quot;This newest part of Canada (separate as of 1999 in the Autumn World)&quot; which is confusing. The first part makes it sound like Nunavut joined Canada in 1999, and the bracketed section makes it sound like Nunavut left Canada in 1999 neither of which are true?<br /> <br /> Perhaps &quot;This newest Canadian territory (separate as of 1999 in the Autumn World)&quot; would be clearer?<br /> <br /> Then - still page 72 - The Fiefs of Bright Paradise: <br /> <br /> &quot;Although Concordia has tried repeatedly to claim these lands, they manage to elude <u>the</u> rule by a continent-based government.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the underlined &quot;the&quot; should be deleted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-07-2017, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:48:10-07:00","id":1089320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imbalance<br /> When a character\u2019s Nightmare rating reaches 10, the player<br /> removes all the Nightmare points from the character sheet and<br /> then marks an imbalance by circling the character\u2019s rightmost<br /> Willpower box (underneath the last dot of Willpower, reading<br /> left to right). The Willpower point represented by that box<br /> functions normally, except that the character suffers a Bedlam<br /> Threshold (p. 294) if she spends the Imbalanced point of Will<br /> power. If all of a character\u2019s Willpower becomes Imbalanced,<br /> she is lost to Bedlam. Marking an Imbalanced Willpower also<br /> regains one point of Glamour. </div> </div> </div>Why not leftmost?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it make more sense?The more Willpower you have the easier it is for you to keep Bedlam in check?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:20:03-07:00","id":1089377,"title":"","content":"The rules are quite indecisive on Aggravated damage. Page 290 says agg cannot be healed by magic, Page 226 claims that Spring 3 heals agg, and Page 187 doesn't distinguish between physical damage types when describing Regeneration (which is admittedly a 7 point merit)<br /> <br /> The Sidhe's Curse flaw (Page 189) needs editing for flavour now only one type of Sidhe gets it by default. Could it be that your non-Sidhe is also an Arcadian?<br /> <br /> In the PDF index, typically visible in the left bar depending on pdf reader, Chapter 4 has an index entry for Contract and no other art.<br /> <br /> The description of Oakenshield has always confused people in my current game. I cast it on a Mauled character last game session and they ... now have marked health levels below unmarked ones? I tend to describe it as a barrier with health levels of its own.<br /> <br /> Autumn 1 doesn't specify the duration. Maybe other arts too? Haven't checked.<br /> <br /> Should there be a +1 difficulty for cantrips cast without a bunk? Is it possible to cast without a bunk? Just asking.<br /> <br /> Page 196 Step 3 specifies a glamour cost for modifier realms that isn't described in Page 194 Cantrip Glamour Cost. I think they were probably written by different writers and the writer for 196 got confused by the phrase &quot;a Realm or level of a Realm the character does not possess&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:56:23-07:00","id":1089401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1088913#post1088913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the problem people may have with this birthright is they mistakenly equate it with being roofied or made drunk against their will, which IMO goes against the intent of the authors. I prefer to equate it with being presented with the opportunity to indulge in an incredibly appealing sensual stimulus. Think of an incredibly sexy and charming person of the gender you find attractive walking up to you, with the food you most fancy in the world, and the music you prefer playing. In normal conditions, the temptation to indulge would be overwhelming, yet if the person truly wants to, they can resist and turn down the offer.<br /> <br /> On your second point, yes, the Dreaming absolutely does not play favorites for humans or their ethical expectations, nor it can reasonably expected to. It does not have a problem with the Fomorian Dream getting dominant again, and it is so vast and ancient it spans the whole psychic imprint of history and the world, so it would be silly to expect it would pay special regard to 21st century ideas about consent. Given how many of its features reflect the archetypes of power, violence, domination, and seduction, and how much these archetypes are fundamental to human/cosmic collective consciousness, It is only to be expected that several of the manifestations it spawns may have creepy and violating implications. We may choose not to give explicit representation to these aspects at our tables, but it is unreasonable to expect they wouldn't exist somewhere in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's likely on purpose that it's in there that way. (If it's 'right' or not is a moral question) If you remember, in the older books the Unseelie satyrs had 'secret herbs' that... _WERE_ Roofies. Not throwing rocks, but that's simply what they were. If memory serves not only did they erace inhibitions but also took away dots of intelligence while under their influence.<br /> <br /> So it's possible if not likely that it's 'intended to be there'... as a rather dark option.<br /> <br /> I.E. A seelie satyr wouldn't use it like roofies but just gently edging back inhibition to let people have a good time.<br /> <br /> Unseelie, or Shadowcourt Satyrs would use it more like traditional roofies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13383-johnnie-rico","name":"Johnnie Rico","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:12:30-07:00","id":1089419,"title":"","content":"The write-up on trolls says unseelie trolls are called Ogres, but the Troll Thallain equivalent are Ogres. Is this intentional? Given the cultural relationship between Trolls and Thallain Ogres this seems like it would be really confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:13:51-07:00","id":1089421,"title":"","content":"Error:<br /> <br /> Page 116<br /> <br /> &quot;Many of the existing Birthrights, including a pooka\u2019s ability to shapeshift, a piskey\u2019s talent for vanishing, and a sluagh\u2019s prowess for slithering into tight places fall into this category.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Piskey's don't vanish. That's the Clurichaun. Piskey's blend in. Clurichaun vanish in the twinkeling of an eye.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also pertaining to the Clurichaun<br /> <br /> Page 90, In their write up there's mention to their 'old' power of being able to read a room and knowing exactly what to say. That power has dissapeared and changed to the instigation of a brawl.<br /> It was rather a large part o the kith previously, knowing what just to say for good or ill. Now it seems to have molded into &quot;Instigating a fight&quot;<br /> <br /> But the write up for the kith (And sprinkled through out the book) Refer to the 'old' power from the previous editions as if the Clurichaun still possessed the previous birthright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13383-johnnie-rico","name":"Johnnie Rico","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T17:34:18-07:00","id":1089485,"title":"","content":"Page 479<br /> <br /> Backer names.<br /> <br /> King Loki Stark, House Stark<br /> Holly Cuileann<br /> <br /> Are fine with out the quotation marks and numbers. Those were just to differentiate them in the backer kit thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13383-johnnie-rico","name":"Johnnie Rico","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:37:28-07:00","id":1089514,"title":"","content":"Page 405: While being obtuse with myself about which Medicine Trait was meant in the sidebar on Nunnehi chargen, I want to field the possibility that having Nunnehi call Glamour Medicine and Menehune call it Mana might be not such great ideas. That aside, on page 420, it references the two being able to bring others into the Upper World by spending Glamour, rather than Medicine or Mana. The term &quot;tribal fae&quot; strikes me with vague unease as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-08-2017, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T19:12:16-07:00","id":1089528,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 193, quote attribution:</b> &quot;Peter Pan and Wendy&quot; should be in italics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:28:11-07:00","id":1089624,"title":"","content":"Something minor I noticed in the nunnehi section page 410. In regard to the Saguaro Totem the name Papago is not one used by the tribe. That was a Spanish name derived from what other tribes called them. The name should be changed to Tohono O'odham.<br /> <br /> Not so keen on the Troll birthright Titan's Power being based on oath taking. Seems as though their very nature of being born from strength was how it was presented in the original setting. I would see greedy folk saying, &quot;Ah...yes. I clearly have two Oaths and so have my Titan's Power maxed out already.&quot; Perhaps something basing it on the Seeming age group?<br /> <br /> I believe it was said in an earlier post that the Scathach became Seelie and Danaan became Unseelie. Was that to have things a neat and orderly even split? I don't necessarily agree with that change. Fundamentally changes their nature in the grand scheme. But then again I saw the text mentions their association being nominal only. Plus until now Danaan was semi official errata...so it is at least good to see them present for roll call.<br /> <br /> There is also the matter of several House Boons changing. Eiluned lost their Cantrip casting benefit. Liam lost their Cantrip casting toward mortals benefit. I skimmed this section so there may be more that I have not observed.<br /> <br /> However, I must confess that the Dougal Flaw is brilliant now. Took a page from the Metabarons in the way that they must sacrifice their body to belong. Dougal wasn't Hephaestus and crippled early on...he sacrificed himself in the forge birthing of steel. Distinguishes them nicely from the Balor deformities. Still I think that aspect of them should be embraced in some fashion though. Maybe a mention of their acceptance of disability as something to overcome through craftwork?<br /> <br /> I love the inclusion of Unleashing and the collecting of all the goodies under one roof with regard to Kith, Houses, Arts, Gallain, Thallain, and the Dark-kin. New artwork is pretty boss too.<br /> <br /> All in all rolling with the changes....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","user":"KyleFianna","date":". 05-08-2017, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:22:08-07:00","id":1089636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnnie Rico</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1089421#post1089421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also pertaining to the Clurichaun<br /> <br /> Page 90, In their write up there's mention to their 'old' power of being able to read a room and knowing exactly what to say. That power has dissapeared and changed to the instigation of a brawl.<br /> It was rather a large part o the kith previously, knowing what just to say for good or ill. Now it seems to have molded into &quot;Instigating a fight&quot;<br /> <br /> But the write up for the kith (And sprinkled through out the book) Refer to the 'old' power from the previous editions as if the Clurichaun still possessed the previous birthright.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't got to read this section yet, but I find it very sad that the clurichaun's birthright is so reduced. Too bad.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:26:24-07:00","id":1089637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vikinzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1089419#post1089419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The write-up on trolls says unseelie trolls are called Ogres, but the Troll Thallain equivalent are Ogres. Is this intentional? Given the cultural relationship between Trolls and Thallain Ogres this seems like it would be really confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the old books, yes it was. In fact, I remember that the trolls kind of used &quot;ogres&quot; to call their Unseelie counterparts as an insult, knowing how degrading it was to compare them with actual ogres.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:59:07-07:00","id":1089651,"title":"","content":"On p. 27, in the Introduction, Fae and Faeries are capitalized, but in the history section of chapter 1 they're not (p. 32a), to my greatest relief. I don't think that fae and faeries should be capitalized. Part of the appeal of Changeling is that it uses material from folklore and legends that everybody know. So no need to capitalize &quot;fae&quot; or &quot;faerie&quot;, even when it is about the True Fae (and only this expression, peculiar to C:tD needs to be capitalized). Also, Faerie needs capitalization when it is the fabled land of the fae (another word for Arcadia).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T02:26:38-07:00","id":1089663,"title":"","content":"Oh dear...my apologies to the moderator. I should clearly read the details of the thread heading before offering rules opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:58:32-07:00","id":1089732,"title":"","content":"It looks like the backer name entries didn't get any human review. My entry on page 478 has a parenthetical note that was supposed to be ignored. Please remove it.<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of entries have leading and trailing quotation marks that probably should have been stripped out. Others (like the first column of page 479) have numbers. If you're only supposed to get one entry, they should probably be joined with an ampersand.<br /> <br /> Lastly (for now, anyway)... some sections have three-dot divisions within them, but no indication of why they're split up that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13372-timothy-j-lanza","name":"Timothy J. Lanza","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:23:19-07:00","id":1089743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urtoroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1087603#post1087603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Relating to this, but not being an errata, is curious how in Iberia, Galicia is ignored, while being soooo related with the Hibernia (Ireland) as it is. At least I have a huge campaign with the Spanish North Western provinces as setting...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It might be forgetten, what makes you think it's ignored? I see Armenia and Poland missed too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:31:48-07:00","id":1089770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salih Bu\u011fra Algan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1089743#post1089743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It might be forgetten, what makes you think it's ignored? I see Armenia and Poland missed too</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it is missed, this can classify as an errata, but as long as I don't think so, I find &quot;ignored&quot; a most proper definition, adding to the fact that almost every other spanish region is covered. Of course, you can call it what you will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And never dare to tell a Galician that Galicia is &quot;part of Kingdom of Leone&quot;. You can be in deep deep trouble xDDD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13370-urtoroth","name":"Urtoroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13370_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:59:39-07:00","id":1089784,"title":"","content":"Page 55<br /> &quot;Nervosa come in an innumerable number of permutations, each one different then the last&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;Nervosa come in an innumerable number of permutations, each one different THAN the last&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T08:05:40-07:00","id":1089788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1089636#post1089636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't got to read this section yet, but I find it very sad that the clurichaun's birthright is so reduced. Too bad.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well the overall sum of the Clurichaun feel better over all now. But it was an interesting change that seems to play into the 'irish brawler' sterotype a bit. Still like the kith but was a bit confused as to the narrower focus of the birthright and.... -how- that narrower focus was defined.<br /> <br /> If nothing else it seems to be a later addition/modification, because as noted the 'former/previous' birthright is mentioned more than once, as if it's still in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13383-johnnie-rico","name":"Johnnie Rico","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T08:34:44-07:00","id":1089803,"title":"","content":"Page 80 - Kingdom of Nubia - &quot;King Biniam Desta (Fortunate Son of Joy), an eshu wildling&quot; - should this be either wilder or childling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T09:48:01-07:00","id":1089839,"title":"","content":"Page 59:<br /> &quot;A pooka taking pride his animalistic features&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;A pooka taking pride IN his animalistic features&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T10:11:47-07:00","id":1089843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1089636#post1089636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't got to read this section yet, but I find it very sad that the clurichaun's birthright is so reduced. Too bad.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It does give them a VERY different feel overall as a Kith. They've sort of been reduced to stereotypical Irish hooligans. Likewise, their Maudlin frailty of earlier made a lot of sense for a house fae that often WAS associated with wine cellars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T10:20:43-07:00","id":1089847,"title":"","content":"on Acrobat, under bookmarks...<br /> <br /> it lists Contract, but no Other Art's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:20:12-07:00","id":1089883,"title":"","content":"Page 449 - About the Morganed kith: Morganed is the plural of the masculine form of the word, the singular being Morgan. A female Morgan would be a Morgan\u00e8s, with the plural being Morganezed.<br /> That's kind of nitpicking though.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Enregistrer</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 05-08-2017, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:29:50-07:00","id":1089891,"title":"","content":"Page 87 -Kith - &quot;The fae were born from the ancient dreams of mortals, and dreams <u>takes</u> many forms&quot; - should be &quot;take&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:55:22-07:00","id":1089907,"title":"","content":"Page 281 - In Normal Defense vs. Desperate defense, it is not mentioned what happens if one does not defend successful in desperate defense.<br /> <br /> Page 290 - What is the rate of healing for physical damages in dreaming?<br /> <br /> Page 269, 270 - In gaining banality part, a below chart mentioned, but it is for mortals, I suppose. There are elements for effects on changelings but which effect goes where is missing (a missing table I guess).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","user":"KokoroWatari","date":". 05-08-2017, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T17:03:53-07:00","id":1090032,"title":"","content":"Inanimae section, slivers are... a problem. Someone else mentioned issues with them being Unleash-only. In the old system they had their own cantrips, all flavored by the elements. To have them Unleashed-only is bad bad bad. For one Inanimae suffer from banality worse (it really messes them up) and having them go Unleashed-only without any way to control the effects or lessen the Nightmare Die stuff is going to cause problems. Think this section not only needs errrata but re-thinking.<br /> <br /> In real errata for inanimae, their Slivers are chimerical unless they call upon the Wyrd. This is a problem because they can only Unleash, and Unleashing forces you to immediately call upon the Wyrd and take your true shape, and all effects become immediately real. <br /> <br /> Mannikins take extra banality from sources may be an errata, because their write-up mentions they move more comfortably among the Autumn. This could be fixed by re-writing the fluff, making it so they like being around people more, but their closeness to humanity also makes them more susceptible to Banality (aka becoming a real boy!!!!). Also, no mention of how Gladeling Mannikins exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T17:18:26-07:00","id":1090045,"title":"","content":"Less errata and more concern in general, but alot of the Gallian birthrights got dumbed down or outright replaced when they shouldn't have, and some of the changes were pretty severe; I'm especially looking at the changes where almost magical powers were simply replaced with merits that make little sense. Oneids loosing their captivating songs and replacing it with just a merit that soaks some banality (which REALLY doesn't work for a phylia prone to depression)... Some of the changes just really make little sense especially when combined with their fluff. Inanimae and hsien suffer the worse from this, but even some of the darkkin and nunnehi have this issue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:00:27-07:00","id":1090065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagusRogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1090032#post1090032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In real errata for inanimae, their Slivers are chimerical unless they call upon the Wyrd. This is a problem because they can only Unleash, and Unleashing forces you to immediately call upon the Wyrd and take your true shape, and all effects become immediately real.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought about that actually. That makes it incredibly difficult to play the hidden elemental model portrayed in the Inanimae book as everything they do fully exposes them to the eyes of reality now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12419,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","user":"vikinzer","date":". 05-08-2017, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T01:08:20-07:00","id":1090169,"title":"","content":"Page 455 - The line: &quot;The Mists never come for their memories of the Kithain.&quot; I believe this should reference Kinain instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1862-inemeq","name":"iNemeq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T02:41:54-07:00","id":1090191,"title":"","content":"Page 417 - The Kokua quote \u201cNone enter our borders without use knowing. And none leave without our permission.\u201d Should probably be &quot;without <b>US </b>knowing&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1862-inemeq","name":"iNemeq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T03:29:41-07:00","id":1090205,"title":"","content":"A clarification might be in order about what happens if you try to use multiple levels of Time in one cantrip. For example, if I cast a spell which will take effect in ten minutes and last three times the normal duration, is that just an application of Time 2? Is it an application of Time 1, adding +1 difficulty and Time 2 adding a second +1 difficulty for a total of +2? Might it even be considered an application of Time 3 (2+1)?<br /> <br /> This is just what I'm coming up with off the top of my head. I think a line of text in the book could solve the ambiguity.<br /> <br /> Also, the character in A Desperate Escape appears to be rolling one nightmare dice too many (or in the wrong order, if the 10 giving her an additional nightmare means it gets rolled immediately)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T06:11:32-07:00","id":1090257,"title":"","content":"Since it's been clarified that Nightmare Dice have nothing to do with Nightmare Legacies and Nightmare Realms, but rather Bedlam, can we call them something else to avoid confusion? Maybe Wyld Dice, as they represent Glamour going, well, wild and out of control.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming Derangements have been intentionally left out? I'm glad. Maybe, in a later supplement, we could implement the old Nightmare Flaws system as a replacement for Derangements instead? That would be more flavoursome and would let us retain that legacy element without confusing things with Bedlam as per the new Nightmare Dice system. Instead, Nightmare Flaws would represent a fracturing psyche, as fae slowly become more like the primal things of fear, anger and pain that form the Fomorian Dream. Meanwhile, Bedlam would be a result of losing control, which is something subtly different.<br /> <br /> Edit: Charlie has just explained that the name can't be changed for nostalgia reasons. So ignore this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-09-2017, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T06:32:08-07:00","id":1090265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1090257#post1090257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Charlie has just explained that the name can't be changed for nostalgia reasons. So ignore this.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think it needs a name change, keep it here. Who knows what'll happen!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T06:55:04-07:00","id":1090273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1090265#post1090265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you think it needs a name change, keep it here. Who knows what'll happen!</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. I guess I'm greedy. I want Nightmare Flaws AND a solid system for Bedlam. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T11:10:12-07:00","id":1090373,"title":"","content":"So I wasn't originally going to post this, but someone who saw me mention it elsewhere urged me to so I figure worst case scenario it gets ignored.<br /> <br /> There are a couple places where non western Fae are centered around European identity and cultural artifacts unecessarily and it makes me a little reticent to invite players from those cultures to play the game. I'm not talking about the big stuff that's been talked about over the history of the game because I know the writers didn't have leeway to just scrap the big stuff. I mean the couple of places where C20 actually drew stronger ties between non European cultures and the European framing of the game. I'm going to list the places where that can be minimized with a few word changes here, and I hope that they are at least considered.<br /> <br /> Page 376-377 The Huaka'i Po make several references to the Fomorians. I know that actually changing the name of the Fomorians isn't going to happen here, but just calling them the Elder Dark when they come up in reference to non Western Changelings will go a long way towards avoiding people of Non European descent reading this and having that cognitive moment when their culture is wrapped up in a myth that is from the Irish Book of Invasions. No matter how it's framed here (and I mean even in C20 it's a pretty clear invocation of the invasion cycle) that existing reference lingers. It may even be an opportunity to drop some hook about the Elder Dark are known by other names around the world, and were no more monolithic than mordern Fair Folk are. <br /> <br /> Page 394 The sidebar says &quot;The Higher Hunting Grounds, the Nunnehi realms within Arcadia. . . &quot; Maybe it's framed this way in a previous book I haven't seen, but I always saw it described as the Nunnehi's home within the Dreaming. Framing the Higher Hunting Grounds specifically around Arcadia ties them up in a European part of the canon in ways that don't seem to actually contribute to the game. If this could please be reframed to part of the Dreaming it would help to make the game more inviting to Native players.<br /> <br /> These changes aren't huge, but I really do feel like they'll make the game a little bit more inclusive.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T12:54:34-07:00","id":1090444,"title":"","content":"Page 95 - Nocker Fix-It Birthright - &quot;The difficulty can range from 5 (for a simple problem in a simple device) to 9 (for a <b>difficulty</b> problem in a complex machine)&quot; - should be &quot;difficult&quot;.<br /> <br /> Page 97 - Piskie Wilders - &quot;While the <b>seeker </b>years make some kiths cynical and wild&quot; - holdover from an earlier draft? Should this be &quot;wilder years&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-09-2017, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T14:18:19-07:00","id":1090476,"title":"","content":"Page 88 - &quot;Unseelie, on the other hand, horde their secrets&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;Unseelie, on the other hand, hoard their secrets&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T14:20:44-07:00","id":1090479,"title":"","content":"Page 91 - &quot;I\u2019ve yet to meet to a redcap&quot;<br /> Shoudl be &quot;I\u2019ve yet to meet a redcap&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T14:37:33-07:00","id":1090485,"title":"","content":"Page 92 - &quot;Eshu seekers often find themselves...&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;Eshu WILDERS often find themselves...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T16:09:43-07:00","id":1090512,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">p.83 &quot;...the many kiths that <i><b>people</b></i> the realm of the Kithain...&quot;<br /> <br /> Probably going for &quot;...the many kiths that <i><b>populate</b></i> the realm of the Kithain...&quot; </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 05-09-2017, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T17:21:05-07:00","id":1090528,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">p. 86 &quot;Getting too bogged down in serious issues <i><b>and</b></i> too busy to chase their fancies means a short path to a grump future.&quot;<br /> <br /> Looks more like differing distractions when it comes to moving towards or away from Banality. Not something where you do both.<br /> <br /> Should probably be:<br /> <br /> &quot;Getting too bogged down in serious issues <i><b>or</b></i> too busy to chase their fancies means a short path to a grump future.&quot;</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T22:00:40-07:00","id":1090591,"title":"","content":"Looking at the weapons table on p. 285 and the Cold Iron notation. They only list the &quot;iron staff&quot; as being able to be Cold Iron. Wouldn't it be feasible to have hatchet heads, stilettos and knives, pole arm heads, maces, clubs...spiked or otherwise, and other such simple weapons earn the notation CI? Seems to me the previous editions mentioned something about the Cold Iron weapons being able to be made so long as they weren't very large. I remember it specifically saying something about the brittle nature of the metal being the main factor of keeping the weapon on the small side. I'd say either put the notation on the items in the chart or do away with the notation altogether and put the blurb about cold iron weapon size somewhere in the combat section. <br /> <br /> Wait...there it is p. 289 and 290 of the C20 book. So I amend this to say to put the notation on the multiple weapons or do away with the notation altogether. It just seems like having it there is to suggest that the staff is the only one that can be Cold Iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","user":"KyleFianna","date":". 05-10-2017, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T01:42:06-07:00","id":1090640,"title":"","content":"About the background.<br /> -There's no mention about Italy and Oriental Europe. Would be possible include some lines similar to the Duchies not described in Concordia?<br /> -In Iberia there's the Kingdom of Le\u00f3n, not Leone. And it's a zone with atlantic weather, not mediterranean. The interior is more dry and cold.<br /> -Volcanoes in Denmark? Perhaps you want say Iceland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T04:16:29-07:00","id":1090673,"title":"","content":"Page 100 - Redcap lifestyles - &quot;The Unseelie <b>pays</b> well for leg breakers&quot; - should either be &quot;the Unseelie pay&quot; or &quot;the Unseelie Court pays&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also this may be intentional, but the clurichaun stereotypes are provided by Micah O'Malley and the redcap stereotypes come from Myra O'Malley. Is there a reason for such similar names? It'd be cool if they were related or something, but as it stands, with no further explanation, it feels like repetition?<br /> <br /> Page 105 - Selkie Wilders - &quot;Seekers in their wilder stage travel the coastlines&quot; - is Seeker a holdover from earlier drafts?<br /> <br /> Selkie Coat Frailty: this states that the coat is only considered destroyed if completely burned or shredded with cold iron. It also says that small rips and punctures heal over time. What happens to serious damage that's not either fire or cold-iron inflicted? For instance it gives rules for ripping it in half. This would presumably not &quot;destroy&quot; it in a manner that would kill the changeling, but it's also not &quot;minor&quot; damage that would heal over time. Can it be repaired? Does it need to be repaired? Will it heal just over a very long time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-10-2017, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T05:56:20-07:00","id":1090692,"title":"","content":"Page 110: &quot;Many call them the underfolk, and rumors persist of vast catacombs where they perform hideous rituals or sacrifice and carnage, but these are just wild suppositions\u2026 at least for the most part.&quot; - I'm not entirely sure here but I think it should be hideous rituals <b>OF </b>sacrifice and carnage?<br /> <br /> Also on the same page: &quot;The lack teeth, their lips are black, and they have small, tired-looking eyes.&quot; - Guess it should be &quot;<b>THEY </b>lack teeth&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1862,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1862-inemeq","user":"iNemeq","date":". 05-10-2017, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1862-inemeq","name":"iNemeq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T06:06:52-07:00","id":1090696,"title":"","content":"Page 106 - Sidhe Wilders - &quot;Arcadian sidhe sometimes struggle with humility in their <b>wildling </b>seeming.&quot; - Should this be &quot;wilder&quot;?<br /> <br /> Page 108 - Autumn Sidhe - &quot;These sidhe are stunning in a human way that makes them more approachable and understandable <b>then</b> the alien glory of the Arcadians.&quot; - Should be &quot;than&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-10-2017, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T09:02:37-07:00","id":1090746,"title":"","content":"Page 5 of the PDF - <i>&quot;Changeling: the Dreaming is the best game I have ever played</i>.&quot; (in my section regarding &quot;player experience with changeling&quot;), at the top of the page, five lines down.<br /> <br /> <u>This should read, instead</u> <i>&quot;Changeling: the Dreaming is the best game I have <b>never </b>played.&quot; </i>(emphasis not needed)<br /> <br /> This distinction is particularly important, as my entry is all about how I haven't actually ever played a Changeling tabletop campaign, because I was doomed to always STing it. This typo actually makes the entire text not make any sense (especially at the end, when I reiterate, again, I never actually played Changeling).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2736-bookmark-ana","user":"Bookmark Ana","date":". 05-10-2017, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2736-bookmark-ana","name":"Bookmark Ana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2736_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T09:18:45-07:00","id":1090750,"title":"","content":"Page 101: &quot;Do not ever place anything in front of a redcap\u2019s mouth you wouldn\u2019t mind losing.&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;Do not ever place anything in front of a redcap\u2019s mouth you WOULD mind losing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:27:31-07:00","id":1090774,"title":"","content":"Page 105 - &quot;Seal\u2019s Beauty&quot;<br /> Shouldn't it be &quot;Sea's Beauty&quot;? I mean... Seals are not that pretty, i'd think...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:35:37-07:00","id":1090776,"title":"","content":"Page 106 - &quot;When the Evanescence brought a new wave of Acadian sidhe to Concordia&quot;<br /> should be &quot;When the Evanescence brought a new wave of ARCADIAN sidhe to Concordia&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:38:30-07:00","id":1090778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luisarmander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1090774#post1090774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 105 - &amp;quot;Seal\u2019s Beauty&amp;quot;<br /> Shouldn't it be &amp;quot;Sea's Beauty&amp;quot;? I mean... Seals are not that pretty, i'd think...</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they meant the singer? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:38:57-07:00","id":1090780,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">p. 94 &quot;A <i><b>nockler\u2019s</b></i> rare smile reveals a row of sharp pointed teeth.&quot;<br /> <br /> Drop the &quot;l&quot;. Should be: </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;A <i><b>nocker\u2019s</b></i> rare smile reveals a row of sharp pointed teeth.&quot; </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:41:14-07:00","id":1090782,"title":"","content":"Page 106 - &quot;The stand tall and slender&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;THEY stand tall and slender&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T11:26:36-07:00","id":1090800,"title":"","content":"After a marital quarrel, please change the Name \u201aTamara Crespo\u2018 under KITHAIN SCHOLAR (Page 467) to<br /> Tamara Crespo \u2013 Prinzessin T'jiamaar aus dem Hause Fiona.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13422-lobezno","name":"Lobezno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T12:48:30-07:00","id":1090824,"title":"","content":"Page 113: &quot;Upon their second oath, the troll gains two extra dots of strength and two additional Bruised health levels&quot;<br /> I think it could be rewritten as &quot;Upon their second oath, the troll gains a second extra dot of strength and another additional Bruised health level&quot;<br /> We've all had THOSE players at the table, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:09:52-07:00","id":1090864,"title":"","content":"Page 118 &quot;The domovoi is then bound that family&quot;<br /> should be &quot;The domovoi is then bound TO that family&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:15:27-07:00","id":1090867,"title":"","content":"Page 117: &quot;If you\u2019ve come up with a Birthright that uses a system that takes elements of Magic and Acumen, use it!&quot;<br /> Should be: &quot;If you\u2019ve come up with a Birthright that uses a system that takes elements of Magic and ACUITY, use it!&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 118: &quot;Likewise, if you\u2019re designing Birthrights, using Advantages and Acumen over Magic can make less work for you&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;Likewise, if you\u2019re designing Birthrights, using Advantages and ACUITY over Magic can make less work for you&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Though, to be fair, i kind of liked Acumen better...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:44:04-07:00","id":1090875,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Bookmarks</b> - The Kiths bookmark is nested in the Seeming bookmark. These should be separate in their own bookmarks.<br /> <br /> Also to keep things consistent, the three different Seemings (Childling, Wilder, and Grump) should have their own sub-bookmark nested in the Seeming bookmark.<br /> <br /> p. 101 &quot;The <b>base damage</b> for the bite is Strength + 2 (difficulty 5)... If successful, the attack inflicts a minimum of <b>three health levels of damage</b> in addition to any damage rolled, and the redcap comes away with a mid-fight snack.&quot;<br /> <br /> No reference is made as to what type of damage is being dealt. Possibly Aggravated damage due to the source coming from the Redcaps' Birthright, aka an obviously supernatural source?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:54:31-07:00","id":1090879,"title":"","content":"Page 89 under Boggan Stereotypes should read as follows.<br /> <br /> On Arcadian Sidhe- They still understand the old ways. Things have changed and they are going to need to learn to adapt.<br /> <br /> On Autumn Sidhe- They, perhaps more than any other, appreciate our service, and they have been here throughout the Interregnum. I respect them for that.<br /> <br /> Page 108 Sidhe autumn I humbly suggest adding the word something for better word flow.<br /> <br /> Ferocious pride bonds these<br /> changelings together. They<br /> have survived in the Autumn<br /> world through<br /> dedication, perseverance,<br /> wisdom,<br /> and hard work,<br /> earning them the<br /> right to rule something their<br /> Arcadian cousins so<br /> often take for granted.<br /> <br /> Page 113 Under Trolls birthrights Titans Power the math does not add up for Bruised Health levels it should read as follows (giving a Maximum of eight dots of strength and nine health levels from from both oaths).<br /> <br /> Titan's Power- A troll grows most in power when they're out fulfilling their duties. A troll gains an additional Bruised health level and a dot of Strength when they take up their first oath, even if that takes the Trait above 5. Upon their second oath the troll gains two extra dots of strength and one additional Bruised health levels(with a maximum total of nine health levels). See p. 264 for more on oaths.<br /> <br /> Page 212 Naming 5 Dot Reweaving this Wyrd cantrip has far too many examples of changing the physical form of living creatures throughout the description of the cantrip for the following line to make any kind of sense. If you change it to a Chimerical cantrip then it makes sense for you would just be changing the chimerical and not physical make up of a living being. That is until the extra Glamour is spent to make it a Wyrd cantrip again in which case it will not make any sense once more. My advice let the realms determine the limit of what someone can and can not do with this one.<br /> <br /> The cantrip cannot change the physical form<br /> of a living creature, but objects can be literally transformed<br /> <br /> Page 218 Pyretics Bunks last line has a typo should be sun.<br /> <br /> or sing a ballad and end just as the<u> runs</u> rises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13408-silvertrod","user":"Silvertrod","date":". 05-11-2017, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13408-silvertrod","name":"Silvertrod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:18:44-07:00","id":1090890,"title":"","content":"&quot;Located on the southern shore of the Black Sea, the Pomeranian Alliance rules much of northern Germany and the Baltic States of Estonia, Latvia, and Lithuania.&quot;<br /> <br /> I believe you mean the Baltic Sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T17:28:05-07:00","id":1090937,"title":"","content":"Having just looked over the Merits and Flaws list, it seems a real mish-mosh. Were some intended to he limited to certain Kiths, because I can tell you a lot of the ones there are NOT universally appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T23:18:03-07:00","id":1090993,"title":"","content":"In the section on Kith Creation, there are no guidelines for Revelry for a new kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T01:30:12-07:00","id":1091017,"title":"","content":"Page 119 - Noble Houses introduction - &quot;A Gwydion investigator might receive the formal title of Lord <b>Inquisitor ,rather</b> than simply \u201cBaron,\u201d for example&quot; - the comma is after the space rather than before it.<br /> <br /> Page 121 - House Ailil - this section uses the Shadow Court in its 2e incarnation. Now that it's been reimagined as a protest movement, would it be wise to clarify this means the hidden movement within the Shadow Court, which I think is known as the Black Court?<br /> <br /> House Beaumayn a few pages later also makes extensive references to the Shadow Court in its 2e incarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-11-2017, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T02:33:16-07:00","id":1091031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silvertrod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1090879#post1090879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">earning them the<br /> right to rule something their Arcadian cousins so<br /> often take for granted</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes less sense without some kind of punctuation before 'something'. It works better as it was, without the 'something'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:09:12-07:00","id":1091089,"title":"","content":"Page 125 - House Danaan - there are no sections on Exile or Factions &amp; Societies. Also a reference to the 2e version of the Shadow Court.<br /> <br /> Page 126 - House Daireann - &quot;Her son, Conchobhair, <b>because </b>a mighty warrior of great renown and unimpeachable honor.&quot; - Should be &quot;became&quot;.<br /> <br /> Page 128 - House Eiluned - &quot;They understand that nobility and secrecy are intimately linked; few in power arrived there without skeletons in their closet, <b>and</b> Eiluned understands that controlling their secrets is necessary for maintaining that power.&quot; - Should either be &quot;an Eiluned&quot; or &quot;and the Eiluned&quot;.<br /> <br /> Page 132 - House Gwydion - Notable Members - &quot;Count Morig of the Duchy of<b> Willows </b>Heart&quot; - Needs an apostrophe.<br /> <br /> Page 132 - House Leanhaun - &quot;House Leanhaun <b>is </b>justifiably well-known as patrons and muses&quot; - Should be &quot;are&quot;.<br /> <br /> Page 135 - House Liam - Notable Members - &quot;High Lord Noman, the ranking noble of House Liam, who travels the <b>words</b> disguised as a beggar&quot; - Should be &quot;world&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 05-11-2017, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:12:58-07:00","id":1091136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beccatoria</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1091089#post1091089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 132 - House Leanhaun - &quot;House Leanhaun <b>is </b>justifiably well-known as patrons and muses&quot; - Should be &quot;are&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also specify &quot;members of House Leanhaun&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:45:29-07:00","id":1091151,"title":"","content":"Page 137 - House Varich Boon - The Houses all have two nicknames, one of which is marked as being vulgar. The write-ups usually refer to them by the non-vulgar name. Varich's Boon write-up refers to them as Puppetmasters (their vulgar nickname) rather than Weavers. If this is intentional, then fine, but I thought I'd not it as (ironically for Varich) it breaks the pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T09:14:33-07:00","id":1091156,"title":"","content":"Page 122 &quot;This I swear, by the blood and the eye, before the Dreaming itself.&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;This I swear, by the blood and the eye, before the DARK itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> OK, This is not a real errata, but somehow if seems... fitting<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T10:13:25-07:00","id":1091188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1087375#post1087375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On p99, the pooka kith frailty reads &quot;If he wishes to answer truthfully the player must make a Willpower roll (difficulty 8) and spend a point of Willpower.&quot;<br /> <br /> To keep their frailty in line with the boggan and troll frailties (the only other ones requiring Willpower rolls, the pooka frailty should omit the &quot;and spend a point of Willpower&quot; clause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, if this is changed, these lines need to be changed to address the pooka's frailty:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">p. 116 &quot;Pooka have to lie when asked a direct question... Yes, he <i><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Oldstyle Std,Goudy Oldstyle Std\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Oldstyle Std,Goudy Oldstyle Std\">can </span></span></i>tell the truth with some effort, <i><b>but remember that doing so requires a Willpower point \u2014 if the player makes the expenditure</b></i>, she is invested in the character being honest in that moment and that should carry resonance, too.&quot;<br /> <br /> p. 116 &quot;Often, characters can resist these Compulsions if the player rolls Willpower (difficulty 8); <b><i>sometimes, as with pooka, this also requires spending a point of Willpower.&quot;</i></b> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T17:53:11-07:00","id":1091353,"title":"","content":"239: Clarice is described as rolling four dice (three Glamour and one Nightmare), but the results show her to have somehow rolled two Nightmare dice for a total of five...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1666-firstborn8","user":"Firstborn8","date":".  added clarity 05-11-2017, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1666-firstborn8","name":"Firstborn8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T18:45:04-07:00","id":1091372,"title":"","content":"Dispite numerous kiths (and equivalents) that can shapeshift and an entire Art dedicated to it, no rules, guidelines or examples of 'mundane' animals exist. I don't want to try and make <i>everything</i> via the Chimera rules. Even just a sign post would be nice.<br /> <br /> There are no rules for regaining Yugen outside a Dragon's Nest. Or rules for shifting between forms for the Hisen. I assume both are the same as the previous edition: (1 Yugen to shift, regain by comparing Chi traits angainst the Gauntlet).<br /> <br /> Adhene have no rules for possession or 'dream form'. Even a note to say 'as chimera ' would be nice. I assume it is simular the previous edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T19:58:24-07:00","id":1091395,"title":"","content":"page 223 uses &quot;Only one attempt can be made to find a specific<br /> fortune or destiny with <b>his</b> cantrip per story.&quot; should be <i>this</i> cantrip","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T23:40:59-07:00","id":1091441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vikinzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1090373#post1090373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I wasn't originally going to post this, but someone who saw me mention it elsewhere urged me to so I figure worst case scenario it gets ignored.<br /> <br /> There are a couple places where non western Fae are centered around European identity and cultural artifacts unecessarily and it makes me a little reticent to invite players from those cultures to play the game. I'm not talking about the big stuff that's been talked about over the history of the game because I know the writers didn't have leeway to just scrap the big stuff. I mean the couple of places where C20 actually drew stronger ties between non European cultures and the European framing of the game. I'm going to list the places where that can be minimized with a few word changes here, and I hope that they are at least considered.<br /> <br /> Page 376-377 The Huaka'i Po make several references to the Fomorians. I know that actually changing the name of the Fomorians isn't going to happen here, but just calling them the Elder Dark when they come up in reference to non Western Changelings will go a long way towards avoiding people of Non European descent reading this and having that cognitive moment when their culture is wrapped up in a myth that is from the Irish Book of Invasions. No matter how it's framed here (and I mean even in C20 it's a pretty clear invocation of the invasion cycle) that existing reference lingers. It may even be an opportunity to drop some hook about the Elder Dark are known by other names around the world, and were no more monolithic than mordern Fair Folk are. <br /> <br /> Page 394 The sidebar says &quot;The Higher Hunting Grounds, the Nunnehi realms within Arcadia. . . &quot; Maybe it's framed this way in a previous book I haven't seen, but I always saw it described as the Nunnehi's home within the Dreaming. Framing the Higher Hunting Grounds specifically around Arcadia ties them up in a European part of the canon in ways that don't seem to actually contribute to the game. If this could please be reframed to part of the Dreaming it would help to make the game more inviting to Native players.<br /> <br /> These changes aren't huge, but I really do feel like they'll make the game a little bit more inclusive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest Kanaloa the octopus god of darkness, magic and deep sea; its hawaiian and deep sea affinity of fomorians might be their connection between two mythologies.(Qyrl was undersea aspect of Wyrm as well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10894,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 05-12-2017, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T01:57:52-07:00","id":1091460,"title":"","content":"Page 141 - Seeming paragraph - page reference at the end is &quot;<b>pp</b>. 83 - 87.&quot; Only one &quot;p&quot; is needed. <br /> <br /> Page 147 - Appearance - &quot;A changeling\u2019s guise often hints at elements of her fae seeming, though she still appears to be a normal, if <b>possible </b>quirky or eccentric, human being.&quot; - should be &quot;possibly&quot;. <br /> <br /> On page 144 - Freebie Point Chart - I'm assuming this is deliberate, but Realms are now 2 points per dot, whereas in 2e they were 3. I have no problem with this change, yay, realms for everyone! But in case it's an error, I thought I'd mention it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T03:20:31-07:00","id":1091472,"title":"","content":"pg.105 Genesis Bell, a selkie painter? isnt she a swimmer or swim team member?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T05:13:10-07:00","id":1091485,"title":"","content":"Page 152 - Example Character Creation - Arts &amp; Realms - &quot;Meg puts all three of her available Arts points into Soothsay, giving her potent tools to ferret out all kinds of useful information. She toys with the idea of picking up a point of Contracts, to play up Saffie\u2019s business sense, but decides that she wants to stay focused for now.<b> Soothsay </b>goes on the list of possible purchases for later.&quot; - Should be &quot;Contracts&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T05:26:59-07:00","id":1091489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1090640#post1090640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the background.<br /> -There's no mention about Italy and Oriental Europe. Would be possible include some lines similar to the Duchies not described in Concordia?<br /> -In Iberia there's the Kingdom of Le\u00f3n, not Leone. And it's a zone with atlantic weather, not mediterranean. The interior is more dry and cold.<br /> -Volcanoes in Denmark? Perhaps you want say Iceland.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also poland, armenia, balkan countries and regional incorrect name for caucasus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:37:19-07:00","id":1091580,"title":"","content":"Page 128 - The subtitle &quot;Notable Members&quot; from House Dougal appears at the bottom of the page, while said notable members appear at the top of the next column.<br /> <br /> Page 132 - The Title &quot;House leanhaun&quot;. &quot;Leanhaun&quot; should be capitalized.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T11:33:30-07:00","id":1091635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salih Bu\u011fra Algan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1091441#post1091441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suggest Kanaloa the octopus god of darkness, magic and deep sea; its hawaiian and deep sea affinity of fomorians might be their connection between two mythologies.(Qyrl was undersea aspect of Wyrm as well)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh. I figure the best I could hope for given this is errata phase is some very basic language reframing to slightly more generic terms. (And that's even a long shot) I would assume whole new hooks is probably out of scope for this point in book dev. I can't say I wouldn't love something like this in a future Gallain book, but those are much longer term hopes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T01:05:28-07:00","id":1091860,"title":"","content":"Page 232 mentions the following:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Players may target a cantrip with Realm ratings they haven\u2019t purchased by spending a point of Glamour per &quot;missing&quot; Realm.</b> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean you don't need to spend a point of Glamour if you have, for example, Fae 2 but are casting a Cantrip with Fae 5, or you spend one extra point, or spend an extra 3 points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is a signature &lt;-----------","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","name":"Shining Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T01:46:36-07:00","id":1091870,"title":"","content":"Page 166 - Professional Skill - it mentions that any skill chosen shouldn't already be a specialty of an existing skill. However, the list of specialisations includes Storytelling which is already given as a specialty under Performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:44:55-07:00","id":1092054,"title":"","content":"This is going to be long winded, my apologies for the painful read: Okay so adhene don't have banality anymore, can't take banality anymore. Great groovy, they're pretty much more complex chimera so, groovy! makes sense, but wait...if they don't take a mortal host, they're naked to banality, and cannot passively regain glamour (Pg.385, &quot;Manifesting in this way costs the Denizen a point of Glamour a day, and in this form a Denizen cannot passively regain their Glamour. Balefires and dross of are thus of little consequence, and only through directly interacting with Dreamers is a Denizen\u2019s Glamour reinvigorated.&quot;)? okay...this needs clarification, how does one passively gain glamour? Aside from a freehold, that is...Adhene don't have Revelry like kithain do, so...what's this supposed to mean? I can understand the not being able to use dross, but whats the implication here? cause it states the only way they can gain glamour is by dealing with dreamers. Uhm, isn't that the same case for every other changeling who doesn't own a holding, aside? So, no freeholds and no dross (which dross doesn't give you glamour anyways, it merely replaces the spending of glamour, so you cannot get glamour from using dross in the first place), where is the big difference here seeing as they don't have any revelry?<br /> Lastly, there's the big undefined &quot;Wut?&quot; in this...A Denizen that falls to banality, Pg. 385 &quot;A Denizen that falls to Banality in this form takes one health level of lethal damage a day (chimerical and real) until she returns to the Dreaming, where she recovers at the same rate.&quot; (please explain this, what does 'falling to banality' mean? tripping a banality trigger?) in this form (See: Manifesting) takes one health level of lethal damage a day (chimerical and real (does that mean 2 lethal per day? Further, you're manifesting so there's no host to take damage here, there's no 'chimerical death' to come back from, this makes a bigger conundrum itself, if all you are is a chimerical being, all damage, should be real to you whether its chimerical or not)) until she returns to the dreaming, where she recovers at the same rate. By Dreaming do they mean &quot;Stops manifesting&quot; or &quot;Hunts down a trod and physically enters the near dreaming despite the fact they cannot walk on the silver way due to the ban, balor trods are one way, and twilight trods are all heavily guarded?<br /> Futher they speak of the evanescent as &quot;Another breed&quot; (Pg.384, 7th paragraph) of adhene, but how are they different? this is not covered, does this merely mean &quot;Hey we've been around awhile and know how to drive things like a stick shift?&quot; or does it mean something more? And on the rules suggesting the possession of mortals...where's the mechanics? does the mortal get no resistance? in the old books it was all about the autumn way, now...do they just 'poof' take over, no rolls no nothing? I have no clue what goes into the idea of possession anymore, and must hereby conclude there are no rules, an adhene has complete power to possess dreamers at will, with complete impunity. As well, Seemings have banality trigger immunities, do any of the aria's have them too, or are adhene not meant to have any protection from banality?<br /> And with the Aonide's Birthright, is Adonis ravaging (Pg.387)...actual ravaging? Because banality is obviously not an option with no banality pool to do the job, so its a manipulation+subterfuge based roll. That said do you risk getting hit with the banality stick for using it as per the rules of ravaging on pg.262-263, like all kithain do for ravaging? and if so do you suffer the agony of banality hitting your host, or in the case of a manifested Aonide, the lethal damage from 'falling to banality' should you botch or fail the Adonis ravaging roll as if you were following the rules for ravaging? Or is Adonis' Ravaging something completely different and despite the psychic rape it does not feature banality in its use and thus no risk of taking a smack with the banality stick? Atop this, there is either a clerical error regarding Aonide, or someone copied something from an old book, On pg 387, under their birthright it states and I quote: They cannot botch Expression or Performance rolls, and are even exempt from the Silver Ban. However on pg. 309, it states the only ones exempt from the silver ban are: &quot;The only Dark-kin exempt from the effects are the moirae and keremet, who took a neutral stance in the conflict.&quot; So which is it? Are the -only- ones exempt the moirae and the keremet and the Aonide's birthright is wrong because it was copied from the old books? Or did someone forget to add Aonide onto the list of adhene that are exempt?<br /> There's no explanations to these pertinent questions, so much is empty or missing for the Adhene that used to be neatly explained. Is anyone available to elucidate? This used to be much better paved in the denizens book, now its very very murky, muddy and has me with more questions than answers.<br /> Oh, to add insult to injury, did someone copy the Naraka flaw from the old books? And I quote (Pg.391): Limited by Geas and custom, Naraka may only possess those of Hindu faith, no matter the method of possession. ...uhm, what methods of possession aside from...possession are there in C20? Cause the idea of simple possession and using the autumn way is gone, confused about this one. Also, 'manifesting' does it have the same effects of going wyrd? IE: If said fuath manifests does he not enter the real world horns hooves and all and cause conniption fits and the mists closing in from essentiually calling upon the wyrd, or using the adhenes version of the wyrd rede? This is not defined, whether it does in fact constituted going wyrd, and if so do denizens get the same benefits of a kithain gone wyrd?<br /> Questions, questions, so many questions....Help a brother out and clarify for me please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13429-joepaine","name":"JoePaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13429_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T13:24:07-07:00","id":1092074,"title":"","content":"pg 249 last roll example, lists Perception + occult to locate the silver path, this should be Greymare no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T16:19:53-07:00","id":1092139,"title":"","content":"A credits switch, plus some alterations, additions, and deletions to characters in the notable members section of a few houses that got a little mixed up in drafts, rather than true errata (more to follow):<br /> <br /> <b>Playtesters (Credits Page): </b>Drop Pete Woodworth from playtesters, add Stained Glass Hearts.<br /> <b>House Danaan (125):</b> &quot;Notable members&quot; section - &quot;Lady Kyra&quot; should be &quot;Lady Jillian&quot; <br /> <b>House Danaan (125):</b> &quot;Notable members&quot; section - Add &quot;Huntsman Jonakr, trodwalker guide&quot; <br /> <b>House Fiona (131):</b> &quot;Notable members&quot; section - Add &quot;Dame Moria, champion duelist&quot;<br /> <b>House Leanhaun (133): </b>&quot;Notable members&quot; section - Change &quot;Baroness Robin, the elusive hostess of notoriously decadent &quot;White Wraith&quot; parties catering to exclusive fae and mortal clientele&quot; to &quot;Baroness Robin, the elusive hostess of the notoriously decadent and exclusive &quot;White Wraith&quot; high society parties&quot;<br /> <b>House Leanhaun (133): </b>&quot;Notable members&quot; section - Add &quot;Baron Tarrow, peerless fine arts patron&quot;<br /> <b>House Scathach (136):</b> &quot;Notable members&quot; section - Drop sentence beginning &quot;Still, even in a secretive house...&quot; it's not really needed, as we're listing famous Scathach aplenty.<br /> <b>House Scathach (136):</b> &quot;Notable Members&quot; section - Drop &quot;Lady Grear, notorious one-eyed Shadow Court assassin&quot; and replace with &quot;Sir Bobby Angel, freelance champion for hire&quot; <br /> <b>House Scathach (136): </b>&quot;Notable Members&quot; section - Change &quot;Kit, true rank unknown, a pooka of the Seven League Knights with a knack for using trods to make surgical strikes on corrupt political systems&quot; to &quot;Kit and Kyra, true ranks unknown, pooka sisters of the Seven League Knights who target corrupt political systems&quot; <br /> <b>House Scathach (136): </b>&quot;Notable Members&quot; section - Add &quot;Baron Bray and Baroness Aife, procurement and intelligence specialists,&quot; <br /> <br /> I recognize those sections might be pressed for space, so I tried to balance additions with deletions, especially for houses that were already cramped. If they can't all make it, well, no worries. More to follow later, especially on the sample character creation front (though I see people already caught some of those in previous posts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Pete Woodworth<br /> -----------------------------<br /> Onyx Path Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13441-writerpete","name":"WriterPete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13441_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T19:34:02-07:00","id":1092187,"title":"","content":"The Hsien section has been a pleasant surprise. They have been given a considerable space, and the developer have put work in doing a good revision.<br /> <br /> Even with that, I have found that they are not clear enough. Please note that I am not a native English speaker, so somethings could be misunderstandings. Sorry for that. Anyway, this is a list of what I think is missing or could be better explained.<ul><li>As some have pointed, there are no rules of changing forms. Does it cost yugen? Which effects apply? Which traits animal forms have?</li> <li>In the previous edition, the Hsien could heal themselves spending Yugen, but I have found nothing here. How do they soak different damage types?</li> <li>As in the previous edition, I find the Rank trait quite useless. Won't be better to just use the Title background?</li> <li>Page 423: &quot;Leadership is now a Talent rather than a Skill&quot;. But in page 163, Leadership is listed as talent, as in other 20th anniversary editions.</li> <li>Page 424: Willpower costs 2 freebies, but since Revised edition, willpower usually costs only 1.</li> <li>I have not found the Yugen cost (if any) of a single I chih. In page 432, in cohorts, you find &quot;Using multiple Alchemies in a single effect is referred to as a cohort, and costs one Yugen per Alchemy in addition to whatever is needed to generate the effect&quot;, but I can't find the &quot;whatever needed to generate the effect&quot;.</li> <li>Page 431: &quot;The dice pool is formed by combining the level of the I Chih being used with the relevant Attribute and the appropriate Chi value, Yin or Yang depending on the nature of the effect.&quot; What is the relevant attribute? Above, you can find two attributes per element, but which one is relevant for the roll is something not explained (at least not without a character sheet). You add the level of the I Chih, or the dots you have in the alchemy? Do you both add the dice of the chi value and use the chi value to calculate the difficulty? <b>A single example of an I Chih, how you build the dice pool, and the cost would be great.</b></li> <li>Page 431: &quot;Some effects are purely centered in Yin or Yang, and must use that Chi value&quot;. Only some? Are there neutral effects, neither yin or yang? How do you build the dice pool and calculate the difficulty?</li> <li>In previous edition, Water Alchemy was able to manipulate air. Nothing is said here.</li> <li>Page 433: Direction fortune. Must the target be in the auspicious direction from me or must I be in the auspicious direction from the target? In previous editions, player usually understand the former, but the book stated the latter. Here nothing is said about it.</li> <li>Page 434: &quot;Speak to Mortals: [...] Humans are made of the same elemental matter and bear the same elemental souls that beasts, plants, and stones do, and as a result Hsien may, through the use of alchemy, address any human and be understood.&quot; Does that mean Hsien can talk to animals too? Should it be explicitly said?</li> <li>Can the Hsien use their magic to heal other beings? In the previous edition it was listed as an example of a yang effect, but then it was never found in the I Chih.</li> <li>Page 431: Degree fortune uses bloomering a flower as an example. How would you do that with alchemies?</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13445-flamma","name":"Flamma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T21:34:28-07:00","id":1092223,"title":"","content":"P. 291 On the Poison &amp; Disease Toxicity chart the column headed by Poison <b>of </b>Drug should be Poison <b><u>or</u></b> Drug","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T21:43:31-07:00","id":1092227,"title":"","content":"I don't have time to read the entire previous set of posts, but here's what I've seen so far:<br /> <br /> pg 244 - How do you split automatic actions, like moving full speed, or even can you? The combat example on pg. 288 also calls out Amphora needing to split her actions if she wants to move flat out and attack, but then she decides not to - so we never see an example of how to do this.<br /> <br /> pg 277 - The grapple paragraph seems to imply that the person *being* grappled can automatically hit the person grappling them for STR damage with no action required. This seems like a typo or poor wording but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> pg. 280 - Reloading - Does this really not impose any penalty in a multiple action? If so, it's not really an action, it's reflexive. And it's weird to even call it an action.<br /> <br /> pg. 286 - The Greatsword has difficulty 5 to hit? In Werewolf and other games it was DIFF 7 so this seems like a typo<br /> <br /> Pg 287 - Rifle, Longbow, and Assault rifle are weirdly collapsed<br /> <br /> pg. 288 - In the combat example, Amphora Invoking the Wyrd causes the bullets that hit her to deal chimerical damage rather than physical damage. However, Invoking the Wyrd on pg. 259 says nothing about converting damage to chimerical, just being able to soak lethal damage. We need to know which it is - since it being chimerical would imply it also heals faster.<br /> <br /> pg 290 - Combat example, casting Quicksilver on Amphora's horse costs 2 glamour - but I don't see any reason why (she has the necessary realms). It should just be the base 1 glamour for a wyrd cantrip, shouldn't it?<br /> <br /> pg. 324 - In the example for Behn\u2019ir\u2019s Sword of Fire, Holly Strike is the 4th level of Dragon's Ire, not the 3rd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13398-fynikz","name":"fynikz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T22:30:14-07:00","id":1092238,"title":"","content":"P351 in the section talking about Wraiths, under the Powers &amp; Weaknesses section. It talks about Sluagh and Eshu being able to see Wraiths. Unless I missed it under the Eshu Kith splat, I don't believe there is any truth to them being able to see things across the Shroud. Any Changeling can manipulate things across the Shroud with the use of the Autumn Art level 5. Even then, that Art at level five doesn't allow for perception, just setting a beacon of sorts. If it is indeed false, Eshu should be removed from the sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","user":"KyleFianna","date":". 05-14-2017, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T22:38:04-07:00","id":1092240,"title":"","content":"Primal 4, Elder-Form Pg.217 - \u200b&quot;Those enchanted with fire become formed of sculpted flame, and inflict one level of automatic lethal damage per turn to anything in direct contact with them. They are themselves immune to fire for the duration of the transformation.&quot; Fire is aggravated damage, always. This is a wyrd cantrip to boot. It should always be agg. Not lethal. The fact later on pytetics 4 (pg 218), also a wyrd cantrip it states: &quot; If the cantrip is used to burn the target, they suffer one aggravated damage per turn. If the cantrip surrounded a protected target with the flame, anyone or anything other than the caster or the target touching the flame suffers one aggravated damage per round of contact.&quot; Also 1 agg/turn? For being on fire? Any normal mundane fire is much worse than that if you get caught on fire, pyretics 4 is woefully lacking for the xp it costs to get it, mechanically speaking in combat, its useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13429-joepaine","name":"JoePaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13429_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T22:43:15-07:00","id":1092241,"title":"","content":"In M20, lightning damage is aggravated and stuns a turn per hl dealt (without having to blow prime2 to and spending quint to force it aggravated, lightning damage is agg period in m20). In 2nd edit CtD, skycraft 5 was agg. In C20th, its lethal, is there a reason why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13429-joepaine","name":"JoePaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13429_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T22:50:18-07:00","id":1092243,"title":"","content":"pg 304 - Mists of Forgetfulness. The chart has entries for duration 'permanent' which doesn't make much sense given that Instantaneous is on there and its how long it takes memory to fade away - Instantaneous should be the highest level. Also for some reason 2 glamour has a rating of memories fade after 1 month, when 3 glamour fades instantaneously. That doesn't make much sense.<br /> <br /> Also, what does mists of forgetfulness apply to - ANY entry into the dreaming, or just the far/deep dreaming? It seems weird that the near dreaming, often right out the back door in a freehold, causes mass amnesia, disorientation, etc. to changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13398-fynikz","name":"fynikz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T23:41:39-07:00","id":1092251,"title":"","content":"P395 Talking again about the Nunnehi. The term Papago appears again twice in the first full paragraph. Replace with Tohono O'odham.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T09:23:44-07:00","id":1092352,"title":"","content":"p. 70a, in the sidebox, for the Kingdom of the Burning Sun, the closing parenthesis is missing after Oklahoma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T09:44:46-07:00","id":1092354,"title":"","content":"Are my backer names supposed to be listed together or separate...<br /> <br /> <br /> I did duet of changelings its listed like (pg 479) Logan Rollins, Lady Rebercca Moonsong ni Fiona <br /> <br /> it should be listed as:<br /> <br /> Logan Rollins<br /> Lady Rebecca Moonsong ni Fiona","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","user":"CameraObscura83","date":".  Adding Details 05-15-2017, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:51:11-07:00","id":1092437,"title":"","content":"I think I have already seen this one reported here, but better safe than sorry:<br /> <br /> p. 108a, under the entry of the Autumn sidhe:<br /> <br /> &quot;These sidhe are stunning in a human way that makes them more approachable and understandable <b>then </b>the alien glory of the Arcadians.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, it should be &quot;than&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:02:28-07:00","id":1092479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoePaine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1092241#post1092241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In M20, lightning damage is aggravated and stuns a turn per hl dealt (without having to blow prime2 to and spending quint to force it aggravated, lightning damage is agg period in m20). In 2nd edit CtD, skycraft 5 was agg. In C20th, its lethal, is there a reason why?</div> </div> </div> </div>This does seem odd given that it's a 5th level cantrip, though it should only do agg if Wyrd. If someone used the cantrip chimerically to avoid paying glamour it would definitely only do chimerical damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T15:27:43-07:00","id":1092538,"title":"","content":"Page 270 We are given Mist &quot;Effects on Mortals&quot; and &quot;Effects on Changelings&quot;, but we don't know how the mists affected other supernaturals. On Chapter Nine we are not told if supernaturals recall or not the fae.<br /> <br /> On Second Edition, Mists did effect supernatural, which limited a lot the crossover relationships.<br /> <br /> Anyway, in the new edition it is needed to know how the mists affect beings not human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13445-flamma","name":"Flamma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T18:46:04-07:00","id":1092609,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>REMINDER<br /> <br /> This thread is for ERRATA. If you are not posting errata, but instead making content requests or suggestions, or if you feel the need to comment on someone else's post, take it to another thread.<br /> <br /> Thank you.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T20:40:31-07:00","id":1092644,"title":"","content":"On page 480, under Liege, please change &quot;Grady W Smithey III&quot; to &quot;Grady W Smithey III, Count of Rosethorn&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13381-prodigal","name":"Prodigal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T00:30:38-07:00","id":1092686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1092609#post1092609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>REMINDER<br /> <br /> This thread is for ERRATA. If you are not posting errata, but instead making content requests or suggestions, or if you feel the need to comment on someone else's post, take it to another thread.<br /> <br /> Thank you.</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if you say this for me, but I thought the lack of mists effects for supernaturals could be an errata, not a deliberate omission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13445-flamma","name":"Flamma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T03:12:23-07:00","id":1092716,"title":"","content":"Think that is for all of us, Flamma. I was guilty of it too. I blame my ignorance of the interface and generally being unused to Forum posting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","user":"KyleFianna","date":". 05-15-2017, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:06:53-07:00","id":1092970,"title":"","content":"Page 161: &quot;You tend to see the big picture, but subtly eludes you.&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;You tend to see the big picture, but SUBTLETY eludes you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:09:54-07:00","id":1092972,"title":"","content":"Page 162: &quot;Given enough time, you can work though most problems that stump others.&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;Given enough time, you can work THROUGH most problems that stump others.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:28:23-07:00","id":1092982,"title":"","content":"Page 162: &quot;You were always picked first for teams in primary school.&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;You were always picked LAST for teams in primary school.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T16:36:04-07:00","id":1093013,"title":"","content":"On the backers name list, it states<br /> \u201cMarcos Almeida Leite Bomfim<br /> T\u00e2nia Mara Bar\u00e3o\u201d<br /> <br /> Those should be two separated names (I pledged the duet of changelings tier)<br /> <br /> &quot;Marcos Almeida Leite Bomfim&quot;<br /> &quot;T\u00e2nia Mara Bar\u00e3o\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3207-devastarion","user":"Devastarion","date":". 05-15-2017, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3207-devastarion","name":"Devastarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T17:20:34-07:00","id":1093031,"title":"","content":"On Page 393 at the end of the 3rd paragraph it say &quot;Much the same way as the Menehune (described later), they learned ways to draw Medicine directly from the natural world.<br /> <br /> I think this should be &quot;Much like the Menehune (described later), they learned ways to draw Medicine directly from the natural world.<br /> <br /> This feels like there should be a direct description of the Menehune's action, as opposed to transitioning to the Nunnehi's action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T17:34:19-07:00","id":1093036,"title":"","content":"Page 397 &quot;Kith&quot;<br /> <br /> This whole paragraph talks about Nunnehi kiths, but on page 393 it specifically says the Nunnehi don't have Kith, they have families. Families was the term used in the previous edition, if it's being retconned then the reference should be removed from 393, but if it is the intended term then the various times the term Kith appears in the rest of the Nunnehi section should be changed to Family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12419,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","user":"vikinzer","date":". 05-16-2017, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12419-vikinzer","name":"vikinzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T19:49:20-07:00","id":1093070,"title":"","content":"pg 266 Oath of the Long Road, &quot;Abandoning the quest altogether strips the oath breaker of all temporary Glamour and a Wisdom point, causes the oath breaker to lose one permanent willpower point and adds two banality point&quot;<br /> <br /> no idea what the wisdom reference is to....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T02:26:11-07:00","id":1093163,"title":"","content":"In the Prelude, there are a number of jarring (to me, at least) word breaks with no hyphen denoting the break.<br /> <br /> Pg 16 - improbable... At the end of the line beginning: &quot;She did not fall...<br /> <br /> Pg 17 - obviously... At the end of the line beginning: the office.<br /> <br /> Pg 18 - ostentatious... At the end of the line beginning: like an executive washroom...<br /> <br /> Pg 18 - electrical... At the end of the line beginning: &quot;Lady Maarika,...<br /> <br /> Pg 18 - revealing... At the end of the line beginning: Maarika rested...<br /> <br /> Pg 18 - lovingly... At the end of the line beginning: the blood of...<br /> <br /> Pg 22 - variable... At the end of the line beginning: years ago.<br /> <br /> I don't know if much can be done regarding this formatting issue, but I thought I'd point it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13369,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13369-chameleon","user":"Chameleon","date":". 05-16-2017, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13369-chameleon","name":"Chameleon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13369_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T02:51:38-07:00","id":1093167,"title":"","content":"pg 449 the hyphen behind &quot;Out of Touch&quot; is wrong. It lacks a space and the dash isn't long enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:55:35-07:00","id":1093221,"title":"","content":"P. 95 has &quot;A nocker must have some degree of privacy when working on chimerical items. Kithain can be present, as long they do not disturb the nocker, but chimerical materials cannot be worked in the presence of mortals.&quot; This is listed for a birthright that is about crafting real items, not Chimerical ones. It should either be removed, or added to the nocker Frailty, as other kiths don't have that limitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T07:12:08-07:00","id":1093226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1086773-c20-backer-pdf-errata-thread?p=1093221#post1093221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P. 95 has &quot;A nocker must have some degree of privacy when working on chimerical items. Kithain can be present, as long they do not disturb the nocker, but chimerical materials cannot be worked in the presence of mortals.&quot; This is listed for a birthright that is about crafting real items, not Chimerical ones. It should either be removed, or added to the nocker Frailty, as other kiths don't have that limitation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can create chimerical items with <b>Make It Work</b>. &quot;A nocker can improvise all manner of temporary, but useful, <i><b>chimerical items</b></i> from apparently improbable materials, such as creating a crude firearm with little more than a light bulb, a water pistol, and a handful of nails.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T09:31:11-07:00","id":1093298,"title":"","content":"Page 167: in Computer 3 text is &quot;You are can use a command line interface and develop custom software.&quot;<br /> Should be &quot;You CAN use a command line interface and develop custom software.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T11:17:52-07:00","id":1093348,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or Skycraft is not about Sky exactly in C20, it mostly focuses on electric from 3 to 5 dot and you cant able to create even a rain or fog with that? I expected smth like 2ed &quot;SKYcraft&quot; at least a power to manipulate weather for a time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:25:48-07:00","id":1093373,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">p. 185 Indecisive (3 pt. flaw) &quot;You must make a Willpower roll whenever your character must make a decision, otherwise you remain undecided about what to do.&quot;<br /> <br /> No Difficulty target number is given for this Willpower roll. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T15:52:51-07:00","id":1093431,"title":"","content":"Page 176: &quot;One Point \u2014 Heroism: Changeling&quot;<br /> <br /> The word &quot;Changeling&quot; is written in bold letters. Should be normal text<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}